{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HwnH8QuMrq63FP91JbXEBA","type":"tool_result","content":"951\t\n952\t| Layer | Recipe |\n953\t|---|---|\n954\t| **VVVF inverter** (Halo 8000) | carrier: square through a bandpass. 0–12 km/h: an async rising tone 300→900 Hz; then stepped \"synchronous\" bands, each a rising pitch ramp that jumps down at the band edge (bands at 12/24/38/50/65 km/h), the \"singing\" that makes Japanese EMUs famous; plus a motor sine at 18·v Hz; volume ∝ traction/brake effort (regen under braking) |\n955\t| **resistor/motor** (Halo 3000) | low saw at 6·v Hz through a lowpass, a growl that rises with v; a notch-step \"clunk\" each power notch; contactor clicks |\n956\t| rolling | noise through a lowpass at 200 + 12·v Hz, volume ∝ v |\n957\t| wind | noise through a bandpass at 800 Hz, volume ∝ v²; louder in tunnels |\n958\t| tunnel | low rumble boost plus a feedback delay of 60 ms, 0.3 |\n959\t| bridge | hollow girder roar (bandpass 400 Hz) |\n960\t| rain | hiss plus random droplet ticks on the glass; wiper squeak/thunk |\n961\t| brake squeal | sine 2.6–3.0 kHz with vibrato when braking under 8 km/h |\n962\t| compressor | thumps at 3 Hz while stopped, after an air release |\n963\t\n964\t**One-shots:**\n965\t- the train: lever clack, EB clunk plus hiss, brake release \"pshh\" at a full stop, rail-joint \"ta-tan\" (noise through a lowpass; at each 25 m\n966\t  joint, 4 clicks for the bogie spacing), points (rapid clicks);\n967\t- doors: door chime, door thunk, conductor buzzer, pilot lamp click;\n968\t- warnings: ATS bell (repeating ding), ATS chime, slip whine, the halo ring cracking (game over), the clock tick (≤ 10 s);\n969\t- the horn: an air horn of two detuned saws, 349 + 440 Hz, through a lowpass, held while the button is down;\n970\t- crossings: bells alternating 700/820 Hz at 2.5 Hz, with Doppler (pitch × (1 ± v/340)) and distance falloff;\n971\t- other trains: oncoming whoosh (a noise swell plus a toot);\n972\t- ambience: seagulls (sine chirps, harbor), ferry horn (low saw), taiko pattern (festival), cicadas (afternoon noise bursts), crowd murmur (a Babble\n973\t  chorus at low volume);\n974\t- UI: menu move, confirm, back; judgment jingles (PERFECT: a sparkly arpeggio C-E-G-C-E; GREAT; GOOD; OK; OVERRUN: a dissonant minor 2nd).\n975\t\n976\t**Departure melodies** (*hassha* melodies): 12 original 6–8 s tunes, one per station, on a bell timbre (triangle plus sine an octave up, fast decay,\n977\ta light echo).\n978\t- Write each as a note list in the engine's note names (`'E5 . G5 A5 ...'` with a bpm).\n979\t- Play it once by scheduling every note as an sfx voice with its `delay` (sfx voices take `delay`), through the sfx bus, so it works whether or not\n980\t  music is playing.\n981\t- Each should be bright, about 2 bars, and end on a resolving note.\n982\t\n983\t**Music** (engine sequencer; `music(song, { fade: 1 })`):\n984\t\n985\t| song | use |\n986\t|---|---|\n987\t| \"Halo Line March\" | title and attract |\n988\t| \"Timetable\" | menus and halo map (calm city-pop) |\n989\t| \"Briefing\" | soft |\n990\t| \"Results\" | variants S/A, B/C, D |\n991\t| \"Game Over\" | sting |\n992\t| \"Parallel Run\" | lobby and card, energetic |\n993\t| \"Evening Halo\" | ending and credits, gentle |\n994\t| \"Commute Groove\" | optional driving music (setting, off by default; driving is about the soundscape) |\n995\t\n996\t- Duck the music under dialog (`audio.duck`).\n997\t\n998\t**Tests** (headless): the soundscape parameter function (v, notch, zone → layer volumes and frequencies) is pure and tested (VVVF band edges, wind ∝ v²);\n999\tevery named sfx and song exists; a browser test counts active nodes after 60 s of driving (no growing leak).\n1000\t\n1001\t### 4.17 Voices: Babble, gibberish in the Animalese/Simlish style (`41-babble.js`)\n1002\t\n1003\t`DH.Babble.say(text, voice, { onSyllable, onDone })` and a per-character hook for Dialog (§3.8 #2).\n1004\t\n1005\t**Syllables:**\n1006\t- Each word becomes CV syllables from a **hash of the word**, so the same line always sounds the same.\n1007\t- Japanese-like phonotactics (ka, shi, tsu, ne, ho, ri, n...), about 1 syllable per 2 letters.\n1008\t- Punctuation shapes the pitch: `?` rises, `!` adds emphasis and a fall, `.` drops at the end, `,` adds a short pause; capitals add stress.\n1009\t\n1010\t**Synthesis of each syllable** (60–110 ms):\n1011\t- a consonant burst: noise through a bandpass by consonant class, 15–40 ms;\n1012\t- then a vowel: a pulse or saw source at f0 through two bandpass formants;\n1013\t- formants (Hz): a = 800/1200, i = 300/2300, u = 350/1300, e = 500/1900, o = 500/900, scaled by the voice's `size`;\n1014\t- an envelope with a 6 ms attack and a 30 ms release.\n1015\t- f0 follows a declination contour with slight random jitter from the word hash.\n1016\t\n1017\t**Voices:**\n1018\t\n1019\t| id | who | f0 Hz | rate syl/s | source | character |\n1020\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1021\t| hoshino | Chief Instructor | 95 | 9 | saw | gruff, falling contour |\n1022\t| mika | Conductor | 260 | 13 | pulse 25% | bright, rising ends |\n1023\t| pa | Station announcer | 190 | 10 | pulse | flat and formal, PA bandpass 300–3000 Hz plus a 120 ms echo |\n1024\t| haro | Haro-kun | 420 | 14 | pulse 12% | bouncy, +3 semitone wobble |\n1025\t| driver | the player (calls) | 150 | 11 | square | crisp, loud, clipped |\n1026\t| kota / fuji / kenji / ren / sato / ota | kid / grandma / salaryman / rival / old driver / station master | 340 / 230 / 140 / 165 / 110 / 120 | 12–14 / 8 / 15 / 12 / 8 / 9 | mixed | as in §5.4 |\n1027\t| crowd | murmur | random 120–300 | 10 | mixed | quiet chorus |\n1028\t\n1029\t**Subtitles** are on by default (they carry the meaning). Calls show romaji and English (§4.7).\n1030\t\n1031\t**Tests:** syllabify is deterministic (same text, same syllables) and its length scales with the text; punctuation changes the contour; every voice id\n1032\texists; Dialog calls the voice hook for each character.\n1033\t\n1034\t### 4.18 Story, dialogue, subtitles, tips (`52-story.js`)\n1035\t\n1036\t- **Briefings** (before each Career stage):\n1037\t  - a modal `E.Dialog` with portraits (`portrait: rig`, a Humanoid dressed per §5.4, expressions via `expr`), with Babble voices;\n1038\t  - behind it, the rail renderer shows the stage's first station at its time of day;\n1039\t  - then a **stage card**: name, time, weather icon, train, stops, best rank, and \"START [✕]\".\n1040\t- **Radio chatter** in play: non-modal `talk.say(line, { name, portrait, auto: 3, modal: false })`, so the train keeps running. It is triggered by\n1041\t  `radio` events (§4.11) or by rules (first ATS, first yellow, first slip, Halo Time ≤ 10, a missed call). Lines queue so they never overlap.\n1042\t- **Tips:** the first time each mechanic appears, show a short tip toast with the glyph (\"ATS! Press [△] to confirm, then brake.\"). They are\n1043\t  remembered in `E.store`, and the \"Show tips\" setting brings them back.\n1044\t- **Results lines** by rank (§5.5) and **game over** lines per stage.\n1045\t- All text lives in `22-stages.js` as data. The style rules are in §5.5.\n1046\t\n1047\t**Tests:** every stage has a briefing and results lines for S/A/B/C/D; radio lines queue; tips show once per save; no line is longer than 3 rows at 320 px\n1048\twidth (`E.font.wrap`).\n1049\t\n1050\t### 4.19 Autopilot (`35-autopilot.js`): used by attract, Dev auto-drive, tests and calibration\n1051\t\n1052\t**Planner.** Over the next 1,500 m, take the constraints:\n1053\t- line speed;\n1054\t- limit boards (taking train length into account);\n1055\t- signal-derived limits (Y 45 and so on);\n1056\t- red signals: a stop target 25 m before;\n1057\t- the stop target at the next stopping station;\n1058\t- slow orders;\n1059\t- the obstruction (when the emitter is flashing).\n1060\t\n1061\t**Allowed speed:** `v_allow(d) = sqrt(v_c² + 2·a_plan·max(0, d − v·τ))`, where a_plan = 0.8 × B4 decel. Target v* = min over constraints minus 2 km/h.\n1062\t\n1063\t**Control:**\n1064\t- If v < v* − 4, power: the notch is chosen from the speed gap.\n1065\t- If v > v* + 1, brake with notch `ceil(req / 0.5)`, where `req = (v² − v_c²) / (2·d)` (in matched units).\n1066\t- **Final stop:** model-predictive. Simulate the train model 12 s ahead for each candidate brake notch, and choose the one whose predicted stop point\n1067\t  is closest to the target. Inside the last 2 m it eases to B1 (smooth stop). This should hit PERFECT reliably. If it doesn't, the physics or the\n1068\t  lag model is wrong; fix that, not the bot.\n1069\t\n1070\t**Timetable (needed for ON TIME and rank S):**\n1071\t- Every 2 s, pick a cruise cap by bisection: for each candidate, simulate the train model over the rest of the interval (0.1 s steps, with the\n1072\t  same constraints) and keep the cap whose predicted arrival matches the scheduled `arr` (aim for −0.5 s).\n1073\t- Coast (N) where that still arrives on time.\n1074\t- Depart the moment the departure is allowed.\n1075\t- **Min-time mode** ignores the timetable and drives as fast as the rules allow. This is \"par\" for calibration (§4.8).\n1076\t\n1077\t**Procedures:** confirm ATS within 0.5 s; make every call at the sweet spot; horn for 0.8 s at each horn board; EB on the obstruction emitter if it can't\n1078\tstop with B8; answer the S5 flash.\n1079\t\n1080\t**Adhesion:** in rain, never pick a power or brake notch whose effort exceeds the adhesion limit (B5 at most with the default 2.6 km/h/s). Plan the\n1081\tbraking with that notch, so the S2 run has no slip or slide.\n1082\t\n1083\t**Skill** (0–1, a dev slider):\n1084\t- 1 = perfect;\n1085\t- 0.6 = human-like: 0.25 s reaction delay, ±3 km/h noise, stop aim ±0.4 m, drawn from `DH.rng('auto')`.\n1086\t\n1087\t**Cheat flags** (attract): no Halo Time loss; teleport between vignettes; forced events.\n1088\t\n1089\t**Tests:**\n1090\t- Skill 1 completes every stage with every stop GOOD or better (PERFECT on ≥ 80% of stops), no game over, every scripted event fired, rank S.\n1091\t- Skill 0.6 completes every stage with no game over on Normal.\n1092\t- Its runs are deterministic: proof hash twice.\n1093\t\n1094\t### 4.20 Attract mode (`61-attract.js`)\n1095\t\n1096\t**Trigger:** 10 s with no input on **title, haloMap, freeRun setup, duelLobby, driversLog, help or about**.\n1097\t- Input means any key, gamepad button or stick past the deadzone, mouse move over 4 px, click, wheel or touch.\n1098\t- The timer is game time measured in those scenes. It is paused while a Shell screen (settings) is open, and restarts on any input.\n1099\t\n1100\t**Loop**, about 3 min, using the autopilot with cheats and the camera director:\n1101\t1. **S0 Depot, dawn:** handle close-ups in the cab; a perfect stop at Mark 1, then the Stop Cam.\n1102\t2. **S1 Hanabatake departure:** platform cam showing the doors, the melody, the buzzer and the pilot lamp; the \"Shuppatsu shinko!\" call with the glove;\n1103\t   then the horn board, the oncoming train and the chase cam onto the bridge.\n1104\t3. **S2 rain:** wipers, the SLIP lamp, ATS bell and confirm, yellow signals, the tunnel mouth, passing Todai-shita alongside the freight.\n1105\t4. **S3:** the obstruction crossing (trackside cam, then EB), the track workers waving, a chase cam on the climb.\n1106\t5. **S4:** chaseHigh with the Sky Liner alongside, the door rush (platform cam), sunset glare.\n1107\t6. **S5:** night headlights, fog, the final approach to Akari Central, the staff bow, PERFECT.\n1108\t7. **\"TODAY'S BEST DRIVERS\"** table (top 5 career totals from `E.store`, or seeded defaults with names like \"HOSHINO\"), then the logo card.\n1109\t   Then loop.\n1110\t\n1111\t**Overlay:** a \"DEMO\" badge, a small logo, and \"Press any button\" with the device glyph. On touch-only devices it reads \"Controller or keyboard\n1112\trequired\" instead.\n1113\t\n1114\t**Rules:** any input goes back to the title (`game.go('title', null, { fade: 'wipe' })`) and resets the idle timer. Attract never writes records or\n1115\tpostcards. It is never shown in hub sessions.\n1116\t\n1117\t**Tests** (headless):\n1118\t- `advance(10.2)` on the title enters attract.\n1119\t- The vignettes advance in order; after the loop's length it is back at vignette 1.\n1120\t- `tap('confirm')`, `press('KeyA')`, `feed('move')` and a stick tap each return to the title.\n1121\t- No records are written.\n1122\t- Touch-only still starts attract.\n1123\t\n1124\t### 4.21 Dev Mode (`62-dev.js`)\n1125\t\n1126\t**Reach:** the pause menu item **Dev Mode** (`menu.items`). It is not offered in hub sessions. It opens an `E.Shell` screen with tool buttons and two\n1127\tsub-screens. Everything works with controller, keyboard and mouse.\n1128\t\n1129\t**Tools:**\n1130\t- Auto-drive on/off; autopilot skill;\n1131\t- God mode (no penalties); freeze Halo Time; time scale (0.25×–4×);\n1132\t- jump: to the next station approach (600 m out), to km (a km slider plus Go), skip to the next stop (arrive PERFECT), finish the stage (perfect),\n1133\t  fail the stage (game over);\n1134\t- time of day (slider, 0–24 h); weather (Clear / Rain / Fog);\n1135\t- force the next signal's aspect (R / Y / YG / G);\n1136\t- trigger an event (ATS test, obstruction, door rush, oncoming, workers, flash);\n1137\t- camera (cab / chase / chaseHigh / platform / trackside);\n1138\t- debug overlay on/off (also the backquote key, once Dev Mode has been opened this session);\n1139\t- braking guide on/off;\n1140\t- unlock all stages; reset save data (asks first, in-game);\n1141\t- **sound board**: play any sfx, melody, song or Babble voice, to audition them.\n1142\t\n1143\t**Balance sliders** (live; the `Dev` group, §3.8 #3), with **Reset to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev')`):\n1144\t\n1145\t| key | label | default | range |\n1146\t|---|---|---|---|\n1147\t| `accelScale` | Power acceleration | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 |\n1148\t| `brakeScale` | Service brake strength | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 |\n1149\t| `brakeLag` | Brake response lag (s) | 0.7 | 0.0–2.0 |\n1150\t| `ebDecel` | Emergency brake (km/h/s) | 5.0 | 3.0–7.0 |\n1151\t| `adhesionRain` | Rain adhesion (km/h/s) | 2.6 | 1.0–6.0 |\n1152\t| `gradeScale` | Gradient effect | 1.0 | 0–2 |\n1153\t| `resistScale` | Running resistance | 1.0 | 0–2 |\n1154\t| `graceStart` | Starting Halo Time (s) | 25 | 5–99 |\n1155\t| `lateCost` | Halo Time lost per second late | 1.0 | 0–3 |\n1156\t| `overrunCost` | Seconds lost per metre overrun | 2.0 | 0–5 |\n1157\t| `stopWindow` | Stop window scale | 1.0 | 0.5–3 |\n1158\t| `onTimeWindow` | On-time window (±s) | 2 | 0–10 |\n1159\t| `dwell` | Minimum dwell (s) | 12 | 5–60 |\n1160\t| `callGreat` | Call sweet spot far edge (m) | 120 | 60–200 |\n1161\t| `limitTol` | Speed tolerance (km/h) | 3 | 0–10 |\n1162\t| `atsTime` | ATS confirm time (s) | 5 | 2–10 |\n1163\t| `comfortSens` | Comfort sensitivity | 1.0 | 0–3 |\n1164\t| `sway` | Camera sway | 1.0 | 0–2 |\n1165\t| `fov` | Cab field of view (°) | 75 | 60–90 |\n1166\t\n1167\t- Every system reads `DH.TUNING` each step, so changes apply at once.\n1168\t- **Debug overlay** (pixel text, top-left):\n1169\t  - performance: FPS, draw ms;\n1170\t  - position: s/km, segment and zone;\n1171\t  - train: v (km/h, m/s), a, jerk, notch, P/B effective, adhesion state;\n1172\t  - signals: the next 3 signals with their blocks; the preceding train's s;\n1173\t  - rules: the limit in force, the next stop distance, the autopilot's predicted stop point, Halo Time, score, comfort;\n1174\t  - the event queue, stage, seed.\n1175\t\n1176\t**Tests:** each slider changes behaviour live (doubling `brakeScale` shortens the B4 distance by about 45–55%); Reset restores every default; Dev isn't in the\n1177\tstandard Settings list; Dev Mode is missing from the pause menu in a session; each tool does what it says (jump puts s within 1 m; finishing a stage\n1178\treaches results).\n1179\t\n1180\t### 4.22 Progress, Driver's Log, postcards (`55-ui-log.js`)\n1181\t\n1182\t- **`E.store`** keys: `dh:progress` (`{ unlocked, ranks, best, stats, postcards }`), `dh:tips`, `dh:board` (the attract table). In a hub session the\n1183\t  client's storage is memory-only, so nothing persists. That is intended.\n1184\t- The title's **CAREER** opens the halo map with the next unfinished stage selected.\n1185\t- **Driver's Log** (large cards, no dense tables):\n1186\t  1. **Records:** per stage, the best rank stamp, score, best stop error and perfect count.\n1187\t  2. **Postcards:** 8 cards in a 4×2 grid. Each is a rendered miniature of its scene (the rail renderer drawn into a 160×100 buffer) with a caption.\n1188\t     Selecting one shows it large with a handwritten-style thank-you note.\n1189\t  3. **Stats:** 4 big numbers: km driven, stops made, perfect stops, calls made.\n1190\t\n1191\t| # | Postcard | Condition |\n1192\t|---|---|---|\n1193\t| 1 | \"Your First Halo\" from Haro-kun | any PERFECT stop |\n1194\t| 2 | \"Right at My Door!\" from Kota | S1: Hanabatake GREAT or better |\n1195\t| 3 | \"Rain or Shine\" | S2 with no overrun and no slide |\n1196\t| 4 | \"Takoyaki Saved\" | S3: obstruction avoided |\n1197\t| 5 | \"Not One Second\" | S4: every arrival ON TIME |\n1198\t| 6 | \"The Last Halo\" from Hoshino | finish S5 |\n1199\t| 7 | \"Point, Call, Proceed\" | every call in a stage made GREAT |\n1200\t| 8 | \"Gentle Hands\" | every stop in a stage SMOOTH |\n1201\t\n1202\t**Tests:** each condition unlocks its card (driven by `debug`); progress round-trips through `E.store`; unlocks are in order; attract doesn't unlock\n1203\tanything.\n1204\t\n1205\t### 4.23 Multiplayer A: AI Hub session, **ghost** mode (`63-hub.js`)\n1206\t\n1207\t**Head tags** (after `<meta charset>` and the pasted, unmodified `session.js` script):\n1208\t```html\n1209\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n1210\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-2\">\n1211\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1212\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n1213\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n1214\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n1215\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Best driving score: stop on the mark, on time\">\n1216\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lever W/S or L2/R2 · Call E/✕ · Horn Space/□ · ATS Q/△\">\n1217\t```\n1218\t(`hub:type` and `hub:players` are catalogue tags copied from the hub examples; `hub:players` is the local count. The goal is ≤ 60 characters and\n1219\tthe howto ≤ 80.)\n1220\t\n1221\t**Flow** (the round is the **Parallel Run**, §5.3):\n1222\t1. `AIHub.active` is true from the first line, so skip the title, attract and menus. Run the boot steps (no key press), then\n1223\t   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [2, 4], card: true })`.\n1224\t   - If it returns `null`, play normally.\n1225\t2. Build the Parallel Run with `DH.rng` seeded from `AIHub.rng('route')`. Assign tracks by seat: id 0 → x 0, 1 → +7, 2 → −7, 3 → +14 (all four\n1226\t   tracks run clockwise for the festival race). Then call **`AIHub.ready()` once, with no key press.**\n1227\t3. **Our own card** (`hubCard` scene), drawn with the rail renderer's `chaseHigh` camera over the four trains at Shotengai:\n1228\t   - the title;\n1229\t   - \"PARALLEL RUN: four drivers, four tracks, one timetable\";\n1230\t   - the goal; this player's controls (glyphs);\n1231\t   - each player in their seat colour (names drawn with the pixel font, never put in HTML) with ready ticks;\n1232\t   - the time left from the `card` event.\n1233\t   - **Enter, ✕ or a click on READY** → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **△, T or a click on MORE TIME** → `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it\n1234\t     back).\n1235\t   - No other choices, and no `Math.random` on the card.\n1236\t4. On `start`: the 3 s countdown is the Shotengai departure melody. At `AIHub.time() >= 0` the starting signal clears and the round begins.\n1237\t5. **During play:**\n1238\t   - every 100 ms: `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: 'quad', s, v, n: notch, st: phase }, { reliable: false })` (10 msgs/s, under the 20/s limit);\n1239\t   - every 1 s: `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'DAIGAKU · 4,350' })`;\n1240\t   - on each stop: `AIHub.send({ t: 'j', st, j: 'GREAT', e: 0.21 })` (reliable), which shows as a rival toast (\"BLUE: GREAT STOP\").\n1241\t6. **Ghost trains:** the other players' trains are drawn on their tracks at interpolated s (smoothed toward the target, extrapolated by v). Each has\n1242\t   its stripe in the player's colour and a name tag over its front within 400 m. They never affect our world: no blocks, no signals. A small\n1243\t   standings panel lists the players' scores.\n1244\t7. **Finish:** after the last stop's judgment, call `AIHub.result({ score, stats: { 'Perfect stops': n, 'On time': m }, awards: [...] })` **once**,\n1245\t   send `{ t: 'done', score }`, and show \"Waiting for the others\" with live standings.\n1246\t8. **`time-up`:** if not finished, call `AIHub.result({ score })` at once.\n1247\t9. **`leave`:** remove that ghost.\n1248\t10. **`end`:** stop input and all sound (music off, the continuous synth to 0, mute) and show the final standings. The hub then removes the game.\n1249\t\n1250\t**Session rules:**\n1251\t- The pause menu shows only Resume, Settings and Controls: no Quit, Retry or Dev Mode.\n1252\t- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`.\n1253\t- No network except the hub.\n1254\t- No chat or emotes.\n1255\t- Options is ignored while Create is held (§3.8 #7).\n1256\t- Storage is memory-only (the client handles this).\n1257\t- `AIHub.fail(msg)` if the canvas can't be created.\n1258\t\n1259\t**Tests:**\n1260\t- A **mock AIHub** in the Node test (`test/hub-mock.mjs`) checks:\n1261\t  - connect, then ready is called with no input;\n1262\t  - play is gated until `time() >= 0`;\n1263\t  - progress comes at ≥ 1/s;\n1264\t  - the send rate is ≤ 20/s and every payload < 16 KB;\n1265\t  - `result` is called exactly once (finish or time-up);\n1266\t  - `end` silences the game and blocks input;\n1267\t  - no title or attract scene is ever entered;\n1268\t  - the Options-with-Create rule holds.\n1269\t- The **real harness** (§8.4): 2 players with auto; 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Each must reach\n1270\t  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\n1271\t\n1272\t### 4.24 Multiplayer B: local Duel, split screen (`64-duel.js`)\n1273\t\n1274\t- **Lobby:** P1 is in. \"P2: press START on a second controller, or 2 on the keyboard\" (`game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin })`). Show each half's keys\n1275\t  (§2). The race starts when both press confirm.\n1276\t- **Race:** the Parallel Run at noon; P1 on x 0, P2 on x +7. `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'auto' })`.\n1277\t  - Each viewport: the `cabMin` camera, a compact HUD (speed, notch, stop gauge, Halo Time, score).\n1278\t  - `scene.hud(r)`: the shared clock and the leader.\n1279\t  - Each player sees the other as a real train on the next track.\n1280\t  - Prompts follow each player's own device."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"eca30f53-226c-4657-a96b-de1a62746d88","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:35.119Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n| Layer | Recipe |\n|---|---|\n| **VVVF inverter** (Halo 8000) | carrier: square through a bandpass. 0–12 km/h: an async rising tone 300→900 Hz; then stepped \"synchronous\" bands, each a rising pitch ramp that jumps down at the band edge (bands at 12/24/38/50/65 km/h), the \"singing\" that makes Japanese EMUs famous; plus a motor sine at 18·v Hz; volume ∝ traction/brake effort (regen under braking) |\n| **resistor/motor** (Halo 3000) | low saw at 6·v Hz through a lowpass, a growl that rises with v; a notch-step \"clunk\" each power notch; contactor clicks |\n| rolling | noise through a lowpass at 200 + 12·v Hz, volume ∝ v |\n| wind | noise through a bandpass at 800 Hz, volume ∝ v²; louder in tunnels |\n| tunnel | low rumble boost plus a feedback delay of 60 ms, 0.3 |\n| bridge | hollow girder roar (bandpass 400 Hz) |\n| rain | hiss plus random droplet ticks on the glass; wiper squeak/thunk |\n| brake squeal | sine 2.6–3.0 kHz with vibrato when braking under 8 km/h |\n| compressor | thumps at 3 Hz while stopped, after an air release |\n\n**One-shots:**\n- the train: lever clack, EB clunk plus hiss, brake release \"pshh\" at a full stop, rail-joint \"ta-tan\" (noise through a lowpass; at each 25 m\n  joint, 4 clicks for the bogie spacing), points (rapid clicks);\n- doors: door chime, door thunk, conductor buzzer, pilot lamp click;\n- warnings: ATS bell (repeating ding), ATS chime, slip whine, the halo ring cracking (game over), the clock tick (≤ 10 s);\n- the horn: an air horn of two detuned saws, 349 + 440 Hz, through a lowpass, held while the button is down;\n- crossings: bells alternating 700/820 Hz at 2.5 Hz, with Doppler (pitch × (1 ± v/340)) and distance falloff;\n- other trains: oncoming whoosh (a noise swell plus a toot);\n- ambience: seagulls (sine chirps, harbor), ferry horn (low saw), taiko pattern (festival), cicadas (afternoon noise bursts), crowd murmur (a Babble\n  chorus at low volume);\n- UI: menu move, confirm, back; judgment jingles (PERFECT: a sparkly arpeggio C-E-G-C-E; GREAT; GOOD; OK; OVERRUN: a dissonant minor 2nd).\n\n**Departure melodies** (*hassha* melodies): 12 original 6–8 s tunes, one per station, on a bell timbre (triangle plus sine an octave up, fast decay,\na light echo).\n- Write each as a note list in the engine's note names (`'E5 . G5 A5 ...'` with a bpm).\n- Play it once by scheduling every note as an sfx voice with its `delay` (sfx voices take `delay`), through the sfx bus, so it works whether or not\n  music is playing.\n- Each should be bright, about 2 bars, and end on a resolving note.\n\n**Music** (engine sequencer; `music(song, { fade: 1 })`):\n\n| song | use |\n|---|---|\n| \"Halo Line March\" | title and attract |\n| \"Timetable\" | menus and halo map (calm city-pop) |\n| \"Briefing\" | soft |\n| \"Results\" | variants S/A, B/C, D |\n| \"Game Over\" | sting |\n| \"Parallel Run\" | lobby and card, energetic |\n| \"Evening Halo\" | ending and credits, gentle |\n| \"Commute Groove\" | optional driving music (setting, off by default; driving is about the soundscape) |\n\n- Duck the music under dialog (`audio.duck`).\n\n**Tests** (headless): the soundscape parameter function (v, notch, zone → layer volumes and frequencies) is pure and tested (VVVF band edges, wind ∝ v²);\nevery named sfx and song exists; a browser test counts active nodes after 60 s of driving (no growing leak).\n\n### 4.17 Voices: Babble, gibberish in the Animalese/Simlish style (`41-babble.js`)\n\n`DH.Babble.say(text, voice, { onSyllable, onDone })` and a per-character hook for Dialog (§3.8 #2).\n\n**Syllables:**\n- Each word becomes CV syllables from a **hash of the word**, so the same line always sounds the same.\n- Japanese-like phonotactics (ka, shi, tsu, ne, ho, ri, n...), about 1 syllable per 2 letters.\n- Punctuation shapes the pitch: `?` rises, `!` adds emphasis and a fall, `.` drops at the end, `,` adds a short pause; capitals add stress.\n\n**Synthesis of each syllable** (60–110 ms):\n- a consonant burst: noise through a bandpass by consonant class, 15–40 ms;\n- then a vowel: a pulse or saw source at f0 through two bandpass formants;\n- formants (Hz): a = 800/1200, i = 300/2300, u = 350/1300, e = 500/1900, o = 500/900, scaled by the voice's `size`;\n- an envelope with a 6 ms attack and a 30 ms release.\n- f0 follows a declination contour with slight random jitter from the word hash.\n\n**Voices:**\n\n| id | who | f0 Hz | rate syl/s | source | character |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| hoshino | Chief Instructor | 95 | 9 | saw | gruff, falling contour |\n| mika | Conductor | 260 | 13 | pulse 25% | bright, rising ends |\n| pa | Station announcer | 190 | 10 | pulse | flat and formal, PA bandpass 300–3000 Hz plus a 120 ms echo |\n| haro | Haro-kun | 420 | 14 | pulse 12% | bouncy, +3 semitone wobble |\n| driver | the player (calls) | 150 | 11 | square | crisp, loud, clipped |\n| kota / fuji / kenji / ren / sato / ota | kid / grandma / salaryman / rival / old driver / station master | 340 / 230 / 140 / 165 / 110 / 120 | 12–14 / 8 / 15 / 12 / 8 / 9 | mixed | as in §5.4 |\n| crowd | murmur | random 120–300 | 10 | mixed | quiet chorus |\n\n**Subtitles** are on by default (they carry the meaning). Calls show romaji and English (§4.7).\n\n**Tests:** syllabify is deterministic (same text, same syllables) and its length scales with the text; punctuation changes the contour; every voice id\nexists; Dialog calls the voice hook for each character.\n\n### 4.18 Story, dialogue, subtitles, tips (`52-story.js`)\n\n- **Briefings** (before each Career stage):\n  - a modal `E.Dialog` with portraits (`portrait: rig`, a Humanoid dressed per §5.4, expressions via `expr`), with Babble voices;\n  - behind it, the rail renderer shows the stage's first station at its time of day;\n  - then a **stage card**: name, time, weather icon, train, stops, best rank, and \"START [✕]\".\n- **Radio chatter** in play: non-modal `talk.say(line, { name, portrait, auto: 3, modal: false })`, so the train keeps running. It is triggered by\n  `radio` events (§4.11) or by rules (first ATS, first yellow, first slip, Halo Time ≤ 10, a missed call). Lines queue so they never overlap.\n- **Tips:** the first time each mechanic appears, show a short tip toast with the glyph (\"ATS! Press [△] to confirm, then brake.\"). They are\n  remembered in `E.store`, and the \"Show tips\" setting brings them back.\n- **Results lines** by rank (§5.5) and **game over** lines per stage.\n- All text lives in `22-stages.js` as data. The style rules are in §5.5.\n\n**Tests:** every stage has a briefing and results lines for S/A/B/C/D; radio lines queue; tips show once per save; no line is longer than 3 rows at 320 px\nwidth (`E.font.wrap`).\n\n### 4.19 Autopilot (`35-autopilot.js`): used by attract, Dev auto-drive, tests and calibration\n\n**Planner.** Over the next 1,500 m, take the constraints:\n- line speed;\n- limit boards (taking train length into account);\n- signal-derived limits (Y 45 and so on);\n- red signals: a stop target 25 m before;\n- the stop target at the next stopping station;\n- slow orders;\n- the obstruction (when the emitter is flashing).\n\n**Allowed speed:** `v_allow(d) = sqrt(v_c² + 2·a_plan·max(0, d − v·τ))`, where a_plan = 0.8 × B4 decel. Target v* = min over constraints minus 2 km/h.\n\n**Control:**\n- If v < v* − 4, power: the notch is chosen from the speed gap.\n- If v > v* + 1, brake with notch `ceil(req / 0.5)`, where `req = (v² − v_c²) / (2·d)` (in matched units).\n- **Final stop:** model-predictive. Simulate the train model 12 s ahead for each candidate brake notch, and choose the one whose predicted stop point\n  is closest to the target. Inside the last 2 m it eases to B1 (smooth stop). This should hit PERFECT reliably. If it doesn't, the physics or the\n  lag model is wrong; fix that, not the bot.\n\n**Timetable (needed for ON TIME and rank S):**\n- Every 2 s, pick a cruise cap by bisection: for each candidate, simulate the train model over the rest of the interval (0.1 s steps, with the\n  same constraints) and keep the cap whose predicted arrival matches the scheduled `arr` (aim for −0.5 s).\n- Coast (N) where that still arrives on time.\n- Depart the moment the departure is allowed.\n- **Min-time mode** ignores the timetable and drives as fast as the rules allow. This is \"par\" for calibration (§4.8).\n\n**Procedures:** confirm ATS within 0.5 s; make every call at the sweet spot; horn for 0.8 s at each horn board; EB on the obstruction emitter if it can't\nstop with B8; answer the S5 flash.\n\n**Adhesion:** in rain, never pick a power or brake notch whose effort exceeds the adhesion limit (B5 at most with the default 2.6 km/h/s). Plan the\nbraking with that notch, so the S2 run has no slip or slide.\n\n**Skill** (0–1, a dev slider):\n- 1 = perfect;\n- 0.6 = human-like: 0.25 s reaction delay, ±3 km/h noise, stop aim ±0.4 m, drawn from `DH.rng('auto')`.\n\n**Cheat flags** (attract): no Halo Time loss; teleport between vignettes; forced events.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Skill 1 completes every stage with every stop GOOD or better (PERFECT on ≥ 80% of stops), no game over, every scripted event fired, rank S.\n- Skill 0.6 completes every stage with no game over on Normal.\n- Its runs are deterministic: proof hash twice.\n\n### 4.20 Attract mode (`61-attract.js`)\n\n**Trigger:** 10 s with no input on **title, haloMap, freeRun setup, duelLobby, driversLog, help or about**.\n- Input means any key, gamepad button or stick past the deadzone, mouse move over 4 px, click, wheel or touch.\n- The timer is game time measured in those scenes. It is paused while a Shell screen (settings) is open, and restarts on any input.\n\n**Loop**, about 3 min, using the autopilot with cheats and the camera director:\n1. **S0 Depot, dawn:** handle close-ups in the cab; a perfect stop at Mark 1, then the Stop Cam.\n2. **S1 Hanabatake departure:** platform cam showing the doors, the melody, the buzzer and the pilot lamp; the \"Shuppatsu shinko!\" call with the glove;\n   then the horn board, the oncoming train and the chase cam onto the bridge.\n3. **S2 rain:** wipers, the SLIP lamp, ATS bell and confirm, yellow signals, the tunnel mouth, passing Todai-shita alongside the freight.\n4. **S3:** the obstruction crossing (trackside cam, then EB), the track workers waving, a chase cam on the climb.\n5. **S4:** chaseHigh with the Sky Liner alongside, the door rush (platform cam), sunset glare.\n6. **S5:** night headlights, fog, the final approach to Akari Central, the staff bow, PERFECT.\n7. **\"TODAY'S BEST DRIVERS\"** table (top 5 career totals from `E.store`, or seeded defaults with names like \"HOSHINO\"), then the logo card.\n   Then loop.\n\n**Overlay:** a \"DEMO\" badge, a small logo, and \"Press any button\" with the device glyph. On touch-only devices it reads \"Controller or keyboard\nrequired\" instead.\n\n**Rules:** any input goes back to the title (`game.go('title', null, { fade: 'wipe' })`) and resets the idle timer. Attract never writes records or\npostcards. It is never shown in hub sessions.\n\n**Tests** (headless):\n- `advance(10.2)` on the title enters attract.\n- The vignettes advance in order; after the loop's length it is back at vignette 1.\n- `tap('confirm')`, `press('KeyA')`, `feed('move')` and a stick tap each return to the title.\n- No records are written.\n- Touch-only still starts attract.\n\n### 4.21 Dev Mode (`62-dev.js`)\n\n**Reach:** the pause menu item **Dev Mode** (`menu.items`). It is not offered in hub sessions. It opens an `E.Shell` screen with tool buttons and two\nsub-screens. Everything works with controller, keyboard and mouse.\n\n**Tools:**\n- Auto-drive on/off; autopilot skill;\n- God mode (no penalties); freeze Halo Time; time scale (0.25×–4×);\n- jump: to the next station approach (600 m out), to km (a km slider plus Go), skip to the next stop (arrive PERFECT), finish the stage (perfect),\n  fail the stage (game over);\n- time of day (slider, 0–24 h); weather (Clear / Rain / Fog);\n- force the next signal's aspect (R / Y / YG / G);\n- trigger an event (ATS test, obstruction, door rush, oncoming, workers, flash);\n- camera (cab / chase / chaseHigh / platform / trackside);\n- debug overlay on/off (also the backquote key, once Dev Mode has been opened this session);\n- braking guide on/off;\n- unlock all stages; reset save data (asks first, in-game);\n- **sound board**: play any sfx, melody, song or Babble voice, to audition them.\n\n**Balance sliders** (live; the `Dev` group, §3.8 #3), with **Reset to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev')`):\n\n| key | label | default | range |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `accelScale` | Power acceleration | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 |\n| `brakeScale` | Service brake strength | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 |\n| `brakeLag` | Brake response lag (s) | 0.7 | 0.0–2.0 |\n| `ebDecel` | Emergency brake (km/h/s) | 5.0 | 3.0–7.0 |\n| `adhesionRain` | Rain adhesion (km/h/s) | 2.6 | 1.0–6.0 |\n| `gradeScale` | Gradient effect | 1.0 | 0–2 |\n| `resistScale` | Running resistance | 1.0 | 0–2 |\n| `graceStart` | Starting Halo Time (s) | 25 | 5–99 |\n| `lateCost` | Halo Time lost per second late | 1.0 | 0–3 |\n| `overrunCost` | Seconds lost per metre overrun | 2.0 | 0–5 |\n| `stopWindow` | Stop window scale | 1.0 | 0.5–3 |\n| `onTimeWindow` | On-time window (±s) | 2 | 0–10 |\n| `dwell` | Minimum dwell (s) | 12 | 5–60 |\n| `callGreat` | Call sweet spot far edge (m) | 120 | 60–200 |\n| `limitTol` | Speed tolerance (km/h) | 3 | 0–10 |\n| `atsTime` | ATS confirm time (s) | 5 | 2–10 |\n| `comfortSens` | Comfort sensitivity | 1.0 | 0–3 |\n| `sway` | Camera sway | 1.0 | 0–2 |\n| `fov` | Cab field of view (°) | 75 | 60–90 |\n\n- Every system reads `DH.TUNING` each step, so changes apply at once.\n- **Debug overlay** (pixel text, top-left):\n  - performance: FPS, draw ms;\n  - position: s/km, segment and zone;\n  - train: v (km/h, m/s), a, jerk, notch, P/B effective, adhesion state;\n  - signals: the next 3 signals with their blocks; the preceding train's s;\n  - rules: the limit in force, the next stop distance, the autopilot's predicted stop point, Halo Time, score, comfort;\n  - the event queue, stage, seed.\n\n**Tests:** each slider changes behaviour live (doubling `brakeScale` shortens the B4 distance by about 45–55%); Reset restores every default; Dev isn't in the\nstandard Settings list; Dev Mode is missing from the pause menu in a session; each tool does what it says (jump puts s within 1 m; finishing a stage\nreaches results).\n\n### 4.22 Progress, Driver's Log, postcards (`55-ui-log.js`)\n\n- **`E.store`** keys: `dh:progress` (`{ unlocked, ranks, best, stats, postcards }`), `dh:tips`, `dh:board` (the attract table). In a hub session the\n  client's storage is memory-only, so nothing persists. That is intended.\n- The title's **CAREER** opens the halo map with the next unfinished stage selected.\n- **Driver's Log** (large cards, no dense tables):\n  1. **Records:** per stage, the best rank stamp, score, best stop error and perfect count.\n  2. **Postcards:** 8 cards in a 4×2 grid. Each is a rendered miniature of its scene (the rail renderer drawn into a 160×100 buffer) with a caption.\n     Selecting one shows it large with a handwritten-style thank-you note.\n  3. **Stats:** 4 big numbers: km driven, stops made, perfect stops, calls made.\n\n| # | Postcard | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"Your First Halo\" from Haro-kun | any PERFECT stop |\n| 2 | \"Right at My Door!\" from Kota | S1: Hanabatake GREAT or better |\n| 3 | \"Rain or Shine\" | S2 with no overrun and no slide |\n| 4 | \"Takoyaki Saved\" | S3: obstruction avoided |\n| 5 | \"Not One Second\" | S4: every arrival ON TIME |\n| 6 | \"The Last Halo\" from Hoshino | finish S5 |\n| 7 | \"Point, Call, Proceed\" | every call in a stage made GREAT |\n| 8 | \"Gentle Hands\" | every stop in a stage SMOOTH |\n\n**Tests:** each condition unlocks its card (driven by `debug`); progress round-trips through `E.store`; unlocks are in order; attract doesn't unlock\nanything.\n\n### 4.23 Multiplayer A: AI Hub session, **ghost** mode (`63-hub.js`)\n\n**Head tags** (after `<meta charset>` and the pasted, unmodified `session.js` script):\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Best driving score: stop on the mark, on time\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lever W/S or L2/R2 · Call E/✕ · Horn Space/□ · ATS Q/△\">\n```\n(`hub:type` and `hub:players` are catalogue tags copied from the hub examples; `hub:players` is the local count. The goal is ≤ 60 characters and\nthe howto ≤ 80.)\n\n**Flow** (the round is the **Parallel Run**, §5.3):\n1. `AIHub.active` is true from the first line, so skip the title, attract and menus. Run the boot steps (no key press), then\n   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [2, 4], card: true })`.\n   - If it returns `null`, play normally.\n2. Build the Parallel Run with `DH.rng` seeded from `AIHub.rng('route')`. Assign tracks by seat: id 0 → x 0, 1 → +7, 2 → −7, 3 → +14 (all four\n   tracks run clockwise for the festival race). Then call **`AIHub.ready()` once, with no key press.**\n3. **Our own card** (`hubCard` scene), drawn with the rail renderer's `chaseHigh` camera over the four trains at Shotengai:\n   - the title;\n   - \"PARALLEL RUN: four drivers, four tracks, one timetable\";\n   - the goal; this player's controls (glyphs);\n   - each player in their seat colour (names drawn with the pixel font, never put in HTML) with ready ticks;\n   - the time left from the `card` event.\n   - **Enter, ✕ or a click on READY** → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **△, T or a click on MORE TIME** → `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it\n     back).\n   - No other choices, and no `Math.random` on the card.\n4. On `start`: the 3 s countdown is the Shotengai departure melody. At `AIHub.time() >= 0` the starting signal clears and the round begins.\n5. **During play:**\n   - every 100 ms: `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: 'quad', s, v, n: notch, st: phase }, { reliable: false })` (10 msgs/s, under the 20/s limit);\n   - every 1 s: `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'DAIGAKU · 4,350' })`;\n   - on each stop: `AIHub.send({ t: 'j', st, j: 'GREAT', e: 0.21 })` (reliable), which shows as a rival toast (\"BLUE: GREAT STOP\").\n6. **Ghost trains:** the other players' trains are drawn on their tracks at interpolated s (smoothed toward the target, extrapolated by v). Each has\n   its stripe in the player's colour and a name tag over its front within 400 m. They never affect our world: no blocks, no signals. A small\n   standings panel lists the players' scores.\n7. **Finish:** after the last stop's judgment, call `AIHub.result({ score, stats: { 'Perfect stops': n, 'On time': m }, awards: [...] })` **once**,\n   send `{ t: 'done', score }`, and show \"Waiting for the others\" with live standings.\n8. **`time-up`:** if not finished, call `AIHub.result({ score })` at once.\n9. **`leave`:** remove that ghost.\n10. **`end`:** stop input and all sound (music off, the continuous synth to 0, mute) and show the final standings. The hub then removes the game.\n\n**Session rules:**\n- The pause menu shows only Resume, Settings and Controls: no Quit, Retry or Dev Mode.\n- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`.\n- No network except the hub.\n- No chat or emotes.\n- Options is ignored while Create is held (§3.8 #7).\n- Storage is memory-only (the client handles this).\n- `AIHub.fail(msg)` if the canvas can't be created.\n\n**Tests:**\n- A **mock AIHub** in the Node test (`test/hub-mock.mjs`) checks:\n  - connect, then ready is called with no input;\n  - play is gated until `time() >= 0`;\n  - progress comes at ≥ 1/s;\n  - the send rate is ≤ 20/s and every payload < 16 KB;\n  - `result` is called exactly once (finish or time-up);\n  - `end` silences the game and blocks input;\n  - no title or attract scene is ever entered;\n  - the Options-with-Create rule holds.\n- The **real harness** (§8.4): 2 players with auto; 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Each must reach\n  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\n\n### 4.24 Multiplayer B: local Duel, split screen (`64-duel.js`)\n\n- **Lobby:** P1 is in. \"P2: press START on a second controller, or 2 on the keyboard\" (`game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin })`). Show each half's keys\n  (§2). The race starts when both press confirm.\n- **Race:** the Parallel Run at noon; P1 on x 0, P2 on x +7. `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'auto' })`.\n  - Each viewport: the `cabMin` camera, a compact HUD (speed, notch, stop gauge, Halo Time, score).\n  - `scene.hud(r)`: the shared clock and the leader.\n  - Each player sees the other as a real train on the next track.\n  - Prompts follow each player's own device.","numLines":330,"startLine":951,"totalLines":1952}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HwnH8QuMrq63FP91JbXEBA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
