{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrZaoKy5Lc6SqZVPwtP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QkyBMSZ7rBvkcT4GqhwjmH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work/PLAN.md","offset":1281,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10269,"cache_read_input_tokens":100049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10269},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"072470d6-9432-4c4b-a710-1cf1389e4651","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:37.347Z","request_id":"req_011CghrZaYDNmjARKS4vSN2D","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QkyBMSZ7rBvkcT4GqhwjmH":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work/PLAN.md","offset":1281,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QkyBMSZ7rBvkcT4GqhwjmH","type":"tool_result","content":"1281\t- **Results:** both score cards side by side, then the winner's banner with Haro-kun cheering. Rematch / Title.\n1282\t\n1283\t**Tests:** `game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })`; both inputs drive their own trains; two viewports draw; two autopilots finish; the winner is the higher score;\n1284\ta tie is shown as a tie.\n1285\t\n1286\t### 4.25 Settings, accessibility, difficulty\n1287\t\n1288\t**The game's own settings** (group `Game`, via `menu.settings` or Shell items):\n1289\t- Difficulty: Easy / Normal / Expert.\n1290\t- **Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox.** The default is PlayStation; its `apply` sets the standard `glyphs` setting.\n1291\t- Lever direction: Up = Power / Up = Brake.\n1292\t- Braking guide: On / Off (default On for Easy, Off otherwise).\n1293\t- Auto calls: Off / On.\n1294\t- Subtitles: On / Off (default On).\n1295\t- Show tips: On / Off.\n1296\t- Stop Cam: On / Off.\n1297\t- Cab display: Full / Minimal.\n1298\t- Driving music: Off / On.\n1299\t- Camera sway: 0–100%.\n1300\t\n1301\t**Standard settings** (built in; don't rebuild them): volume, music, effects, reduce motion (turns off sway and flashes), screen filter (CRT/scanlines),\n1302\tcontrols rebinding, rumble, and so on.\n1303\t\n1304\tEverything stays readable with no colour vision: signal letters, judgment words and lamp positions.\n1305\t\n1306\t**Tests:** each setting applies (glyph family, lever flip, guide visible, auto calls, subtitles off hides the subtitle box); settings survive a reload via\n1307\t`E.store`.\n1308\t\n1309\t### 4.26 Front-end screens (`55-ui-*.js`): big, few items, pixel-art, controller-first\n1310\t\n1311\t- **Title:**\n1312\t  - The background is the rail renderer's platform camera at Akari Central at dawn, with a Halo 8000 gliding in.\n1313\t  - Logo: `E.font.title('DENSHA DE HALO!', ...)` (scale 4, gold gradient) with a glowing gold **halo ring** around the final \"O\", and Haro-kun\n1314\t    bouncing beside it.\n1315\t  - Subtitle: \"THE HALO LINE · AKARI CITY\".\n1316\t  - `E.Menu`: CAREER · FREE RUN · DUEL · DRIVER'S LOG · HOW TO DRIVE · SETTINGS · ABOUT & CREDITS. Hover moves the focus and click picks.\n1317\t  - A prompt line with the device glyph, and the version (`E.versionLabel()` plus the game version v1.0).\n1318\t  - Keep it clear of the top-right corner buttons.\n1319\t- **Halo Map** (stage select):\n1320\t  - A gold ring (radius about 0.32 × min(W, H)) with 12 station dots and labels.\n1321\t  - Each stage is an arc between its stations: glowing when selected, grey when locked, with its rank stamp when done. Haro-kun floats in the centre.\n1322\t  - The stage card on the right (below on tall screens): name, time, weather, train, stops, best.\n1323\t  - ←/→ or the stick go round the ring; hover an arc to select it; ✕ or a click to go; ○ back.\n1324\t- **Free Run setup:** a stage on the ring, plus 4 rows of ←/→ choices (Time, Weather, Train, Difficulty), then START.\n1325\t- **Briefing:** §4.18.\n1326\t- **Results:**\n1327\t  - the rank stamp slams in (a scale tween, a shake, the stamp sound);\n1328\t  - 5 big lines (Stops, Punctuality, Calls & Horn, Smoothness, Penalties) with a total;\n1329\t  - Halo Time left; Hoshino's line;\n1330\t  - any new postcard flip;\n1331\t  - buttons: NEXT STAGE / RETRY / HALO MAP.\n1332\t- **Game Over:** the cracked halo; Hoshino's line; RETRY STAGE / CONTINUE FROM LAST STATION (Halo Time set back to the start value, score halved) / HALO MAP.\n1333\t- **Ending** (after S5's results):\n1334\t  - the finale cinematic: platform cam; staff and crowd bow; Hoshino gives you his pocket watch (dialog);\n1335\t  - then credits rolling over a night chase cam circling the whole ring, to \"Evening Halo\";\n1336\t  - \"THANK YOU FOR RIDING THE HALO LINE\";\n1337\t  - then the title, with S5 marked done.\n1338\t- **How to Drive:** a Shell `help` screen with keys for the current device and 5 short sections: Lever, Stop on the mark, Be on time, Point and\n1339\t  call, Signals & ATS.\n1340\t- **About & Credits:** pixel pages, ↑/↓ to scroll and ←/→ for the page, mouse wheel to scroll:\n1341\t  1. Credits (an original homage to *Densha de Go!* (Taito), not affiliated; my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato, MIT; the AI Hub client; asset sets if\n1342\t     used: Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG CC0; made by the building model);\n1343\t  2. **Source Information** (every TASK.md field);\n1344\t  3. Testing Feedback;\n1345\t  4. Engine Feedback;\n1346\t  5. Prompt Feedback.\n1347\t  - The text lives in `src/55-ui-about.js` and is filled in at the end, the same as the chat reply and `exit-interview.json` (§9).\n1348\t\n1349\t**Tests:** each screen opens and closes with confirm and cancel; the halo map wraps; locked stages can't be started; mouse hover selects (`input.feed('move')`);\n1350\tAbout contains every Source Information label; results buttons route correctly.\n1351\t\n1352\t---\n1353\t\n1354\t## 5. Content\n1355\t\n1356\t### 5.1 Akari City and the Halo Line\n1357\t\n1358\tThe line runs clockwise as a loop of **20,600 m** with **12 stations**. It is double-track: ours at x 0, the counter-clockwise track at x +3.8.\n1359\tFrom 11,800 to 15,600 it is **quad-track**: tracks at −7, 0, +7, +14; island platforms span −5.4…−1.6 and +8.6…+12.4. Line colours: **Halo Gold**\n1360\t`#f2c230` and **Sky** `#3aa0e0`.\n1361\t\n1362\t| # | id | In-game name | Meaning | Stop (6-car s) | Platform | Zone | Landmark / character |\n1363\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1364\t| 0 | akari | AKARI CENTRAL | Akari Central | 0 (≡ 20,600) | island + side, 245 m, big roof | downtown | terminal hall with clock tower; Station Master Ota |\n1365\t| 1 | hanabatake | HANABATAKE | Flower Fields | 1,600 | left, 190 m | suburb-flowers | greenhouses, flower rows; Kota the train-fan kid |\n1366\t| 2 | kujira | KUJIRA-BASHI | Whale Bridge | 3,450 | right, 175 m | riverside | whale-back steel arch over the river mouth (bridge 2,600–3,200) |\n1367\t| 3 | minato | MINATO-MAE | Harbor Front | 5,100 | left + freight yard right | harbor | gantry cranes, containers, ferry; seagulls |\n1368\t| 4 | todai | TODAI-SHITA | Below the Lighthouse | 6,950 | island with passing loop | cliff | lighthouse on the cliff; tunnel 6,050–6,550 |\n1369\t| 5 | okiku | OKIKU-DERA | Great Chrysanthemum Temple | 8,700 | left, wooden, 185 m | temple-town | five-storey pagoda, temple gate, festival; Grandma Fuji |\n1370\t| 6 | yuhi | YUHI-ZAKA | Sunset Slope | 10,450 | right, hilltop | hills | terraced houses, sea view, little shrine |\n1371\t| 7 | shotengai | SHOTENGAI | Shopping Arcade | 12,100 | 2 islands (quad), viaduct | city-elevated | arcade roofs, neon game centre; Kenji's office |\n1372\t| 8 | daigaku | DAIGAKU-MAE | University | 13,700 | 2 islands (quad) | campus | clock tower, ginkgo trees, bicycles |\n1373\t| 9 | koen | SAKURA-KOEN | Cherry Blossom Park | 15,300 | 2 islands (quad) | park | sakura, pond, the \"Akari Eye\" Ferris wheel; petals |\n1374\t| 10 | hoshimi | HOSHIMI-DAI | Stargazing Heights | 17,100 | left | hills-north | observatory dome |\n1375\t| 11 | kawasemi | KAWASEMI | Kingfisher | 18,800 | right | river-north | river bridge 19,200–19,500, fishermen, paddies |\n1376\t\n1377\t- **Stop markers and platform lengths:**\n1378\t  - Akari Central and the three quad-section stations (Shotengai, Daigaku-mae, Sakura-Koen) have both \"6\" and \"10\" markers, with the 10 placed\n1379\t    8 m past the 6. Their platforms are 220–245 m.\n1380\t  - Every other station has only a \"6\" marker, on a platform of about 180 m.\n1381\t- **The quad transition (11,650–11,800):** the counter-clockwise track swings out from +3.8 to +14 in a gentle S-curve, and tracks −7 and +7 branch\n1382\t  off. Do the same in reverse at 15,600–15,750. In normal service, 0 and +7 carry clockwise trains (the Halo local and the Sky Liner express), and\n1383\t  −7 and +14 carry counter-clockwise ones.\n1384\t- **Station kit** (things and strips): name boards every 40 m (white; big romaji; English meaning smaller; previous and next stations with\n1385\t  arrows), canopy and columns, benches, vending machines (red/blue/white with lit panels), sorting bins, a platform clock, LED departure board,\n1386\t  stair housings, a safety fence, door-queue marks, staff at the head end, a Haro-kun poster.\n1387\t- In-game text is ASCII (the font has no kana or macrons), so names have no macrons: TODAI-SHITA, OKIKU-DERA, SHOTENGAI.\n1388\t\n1389\t**Zones** (scenery sets; buildings come from a parametric box generator, §5.6):\n1390\t\n1391\t| zone | s range | ground | buildings (weights) | nature | props | backdrop |\n1392\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1393\t| downtown | 19,900–700 | concrete | office towers .4, department store .2, hotels .2, overpasses | street trees | billboards (Haro-kun ads), lamp posts, vending machines | city skyline |\n1394\t| suburb-flowers | 700–2,500 | fields/grass | houses .5 (blue/grey/terracotta roofs), apartments with balconies and laundry .3, greenhouses .1, konbini .1 | flower rows, paddies | utility poles and wires, bikes, crossing mirrors | hills, far city |\n1395\t| riverside | 2,500–3,600 | water/reeds | boat sheds | reeds, willows | fishermen, rowboats (library) | river mouth, sea |\n1396\t| harbor | 3,600–5,800 | asphalt | warehouses (long strips with roll-up doors) .5, container stacks .4 | — | gantry cranes, crates/barrels (library), bollards, seagulls | sea, ships |\n1397\t| cliff | 5,800–7,500 | rock/grass | fishing houses | pines (library), rocks | stone walls, tunnel portals | sea, cliffs |\n1398\t| temple-town | 7,500–9,300 | gravel | machiya (dark wood, tiled roofs) .6, shops with noren .4 | pines, maples, stone lanterns | lantern strings, torii, stalls | hills, pagoda |\n1399\t| hills | 9,300–11,700 | slopes | terrace houses | cedars, bamboo | retaining walls, guard rails | sea (left), sunset |\n1400\t| city-elevated | 11,700–13,200 | rooftops below the viaduct | arcade roofs, neon facades, apartment towers | — | sound walls, billboards | skyline |\n1401\t| campus | 13,200–14,500 | lawns | university blocks, gym dome | ginkgo | bike rows, students | city |\n1402\t| park | 14,500–16,000 | grass | pavilion | sakura (petal particles) | lanterns, benches (library) | hills, Ferris wheel |\n1403\t| hills-north | 16,000–18,000 | grass/forest | houses | cedars | poles | mountains, stars |\n1404\t| river-north | 18,000–19,700 | paddies/water | farmhouses | reeds | scarecrows, fishermen | mountains |\n1405\t| depot | depot route | gravel | depot sheds (strips), pits | — | lamps, workers, parked trains | dawn city |\n1406\t\n1407\t**Depot route** (S0): 1,000 m on a single track with sidings at x ±4.5 holding parked trains (0–350); straight to 400, a curve R 800 L from 400 to 600,\n1408\tthen straight. Stop marks (yellow boards) at 300, 620 and 900. A staff halt platform \"DEPOT GATE\" on the left at 860–920. A shunting signal at 40.\n1409\t\n1410\t### 5.2 Trains\n1411\t\n1412\t| id | name | cab | notches | traction a0 (km/h/s) | brakes | lags (apply/release/power) | vmax | sound | livery |\n1413\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1414\t| `h8000` | HALO 8000 | modern grey panel, one T-handle, LCD notch display | P5 / B8 | .8 1.4 2.0 2.6 3.2 (vk 15 25 35 40 45) | 0.5·n, EB 5.0 | .7 / .5 / .3 s | 110 | VVVF \"singing\" | silver, gold halo stripe, sky band |\n1415\t| `h3000` | HALO 3000 (retro) | green panel, two handles, analog gauges | P4 / B7 | .7 1.3 1.9 2.5 (vk 18 28 36 42) | 0.55·n, EB 4.6 | 1.1 / .8 / .5 s | 100 | resistor growl and clunks | cream, orange stripe |\n1416\t| `skyliner` | SKY LINER (rival) | — | AI | — | — | — | 120 | — | purple and silver |\n1417\t| `freight` | MINATO FREIGHT | — | AI | — | — | — | 75 | — | blue loco plus colourful containers |\n1418\t| `inner` | HALO 8000 inner loop | — | AI | — | — | — | — | — | as h8000 |\n1419\t\n1420\t- Formations: `h8000-6`, `h8000-10` (S4), `h3000-6` (S2).\n1421\t\n1422\t### 5.3 Stages\n1423\t\n1424\tTimes are initial values; calibrate them (§4.8). \"s\" means route metres.\n1425\t\n1426\t**S0 · DAWN DEPOT** (tutorial). 05:30 dawn, clear, `h8000-6`, depot route, Halo Time frozen.\n1427\t\n1428\tSteps, each a Hoshino line with a prompt; the next unlocks when the condition holds:\n1429\t1. P1, reach 10 km/h.\n1430\t2. N, coast.\n1431\t3. Brake: get below 5 km/h.\n1432\t4. Stop at Mark 1 (300); judged with no penalty; Stop Cam explained.\n1433\t5. The departure call on the shunting signal.\n1434\t6. Up to 40 under the \"40\" board.\n1435\t7. Mark 2 (620), easing to B1: SMOOTH explained.\n1436\t8. EB demo (pull, stop, release).\n1437\t9. Mark 3 (900) within 1 m to pass; retry the step on failure.\n1438\t\n1439\tThe certificate stamp follows, then S1 unlocks. Halo Time, ATS and the horn get one sentence each from Hoshino (\"You'll meet those in service\").\n1440\t\n1441\t**S1 · FIRST LIGHT LOCAL.** 06:40 dawn into morning, clear, `h8000-6`, Akari Central → Hanabatake → Kujira-bashi.\n1442\t\n1443\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1444\t|---|---|---|\n1445\t| AKARI CENTRAL | — | 06:40:00 |\n1446\t| HANABATAKE | 06:42:05 | 06:42:30 |\n1447\t| KUJIRA-BASHI | 06:44:45 | — |\n1448\t\n1449\tGeometry (route script excerpt, the pattern for every stage):\n1450\t```\n1451\t[-230,'station',{id:'akari',side:'island',len:245,stop:{6:0,10:8},roof:[-215,5],melody:'akari',crowd:3,landmark:'terminal'}]\n1452\t[0,'zone','downtown'] [60,'signal',{id:'AK-S',kind:'start'}] [150,'overpass',{w:18,h:7}]\n1453\t[200,'limit',{v:45,until:420}] [420,'limit',{v:85}] [520,'curve',{len:260,r:900,dir:'R'}]\n1454\t[700,'zone','suburb-flowers'] [700,'signal',{id:'B101',kind:'block'}]\n1455\t[880,'limit',{v:70,until:1260}] [900,'curve',{len:330,r:500,dir:'L'}]\n1456\t[1050,'horn',{}] [1110,'crossing',{id:'X1',road:6,cars:3,peds:2}] [1250,'signal',{id:'B102',kind:'block'}]\n1457\t[1380,'signal',{id:'HB-H',kind:'home'}] [1420,'station',{id:'hanabatake',side:'L',len:190,stop:{6:1600},melody:'hanabatake',crowd:2}]\n1458\t[1660,'signal',{id:'HB-S',kind:'start'}] [1800,'grade',{len:300,permille:8}] [2150,'signal',{id:'B103',kind:'block'}]\n1459\t[2300,'horn',{}] [2450,'limit',{v:75,until:3250}] [2500,'zone','riverside'] [2600,'bridge',{len:600,kind:'truss',water:'river'}]\n1460\t[2700,'curve',{len:400,r:1200,dir:'R'}] [2950,'signal',{id:'B104',kind:'block'}] [3250,'signal',{id:'KJ-H',kind:'home'}]\n1461\t[3290,'station',{id:'kujira',side:'R',len:175,stop:{6:3450},melody:'kujira',crowd:2}]\n1462\t```\n1463\t\n1464\t- Events: crossing X1 (normal); `oncoming` at 2,000; Kota waves at Hanabatake (dwell); radio lines (§5.5).\n1465\t- Teaches: the timetable and clock, the departure procedure, calls, the horn board, a limit board, an oncoming train, crossing bells, melodies and\n1466\t  announcements.\n1467\t\n1468\t**S2 · HARBOR RAIN RAPID.** 10:15 day, **rain**, `h3000-6`, Kujira-bashi → Minato-mae → (pass Todai-shita) → Okiku-dera.\n1469\t\n1470\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1471\t|---|---|---|\n1472\t| KUJIRA-BASHI | — | 10:15:00 |\n1473\t| MINATO-MAE | 10:16:55 | 10:17:20 |\n1474\t| TODAI-SHITA | pass 10:20:20 | |\n1475\t| OKIKU-DERA | 10:22:15 | — |\n1476\t\n1477\t- Geometry: line speed 95 (Rapid); curve R 700 L at 3,700–4,000 (limit 80).\n1478\t  - Signals: B201 3,900, B202 4,300, MN-H 4,880 (the Minato-mae platform runs 4,925–5,115), MN-S 5,160, **M5600** 5,600, **M6000** 6,000,\n1479\t    B205 6,600, TD-H 6,850 (main line through, no platform stop), B207 7,600, OK-H 8,480 (the Okiku-dera platform runs 8,530–8,715).\n1480\t  - Tunnel 6,050–6,550 with a curve R 400 R (limit 60, horn board 5,950).\n1481\t  - Pass board at 6,550. Freight loop at Todai-shita on the left, 6,750–7,150.\n1482\t- **Freight script** (260 m long):\n1483\t  - It joins our track from the Minato yard at 5,250 at **10:16:20** and runs at 45 km/h (12.5 m/s).\n1484\t  - It **stops with its front at 6,300 from about 10:17:44 for 40 s** (points being set), then pulls on and diverges into the Todai loop at 6,780,\n1485\t    where it stands.\n1486\t  - What the player gets, at par:\n1487\t    - At our 10:17:20 departure its rear is in block M5600–M6000, so the starting signal MN-S shows **Y** (call: \"Chui!\").\n1488\t    - Near 10:17:56 we pass M6000's ATS beacon at 5,400. M6000 is **R** (the freight is standing in block 6,000–6,600), so the **ATS bell rings**.\n1489\t    - We stop before M6000 at about 10:18:56. The freight pulls away at 10:18:24, and its rear clears 6,600 at about 10:19:25, so M6000 turns\n1490\t      **Y** after a wait of 20–30 s, then **G** once the freight is wholly in the loop (about 10:19:50).\n1491\t  - We see its tail lights through the rain while we arrive at Minato-mae, and later pass it standing in the loop at Todai-shita.\n1492\t  - The test (§4.4) checks this sequence with the autopilot.\n1493\t- Teaches: another train type (two handles, slow brakes), rain slip and slide, yellow signals, ATS confirm, a tunnel, a pass station.\n1494\t\n1495\t**S3 · TEMPLE HILL LOCAL.** 14:00 afternoon haze, clear, `h8000-6`, Okiku-dera → Yuhi-zaka → Shotengai. The stage **opens during the festival dwell**\n1496\tat Okiku-dera.\n1497\t\n1498\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1499\t|---|---|---|\n1500\t| OKIKU-DERA | (dwell) | 14:00:00 |\n1501\t| YUHI-ZAKA | 14:02:40 | 14:03:00 |\n1502\t| SHOTENGAI | 14:05:30 | — |\n1503\t\n1504\t- Geometry:\n1505\t  - crossing X2 at 9,050 (normal);\n1506\t  - climb **25‰** from 9,200 to 10,300; curve R 600 R at 9,300–9,600; curve R 450 L at 9,900–10,200 (limit 60);\n1507\t  - horn board 9,450; **workers** with a slow order of 25 from 9,600 to 9,900 (lookout at 9,550);\n1508\t  - Yuhi-zaka at 10,450;\n1509\t  - descent **20‰** from 10,700 to 11,450; curve R 500 L at 10,900–11,200 (limit 55);\n1510\t  - **obstruction emitter at 11,150 for crossing X3 at 11,500** (the festival's takoyaki cart); horn board 11,400;\n1511\t  - viaduct from 11,700; Shotengai at 12,100.\n1512\t- Events: festival (crowd ×2, lanterns, taiko), `workers`, `obstruction` at X3 (clears 12 s after we stop), Grandma Fuji bows at Yuhi-zaka, `oncoming`\n1513\t  at 11,200.\n1514\t- Teaches: gradients both ways, a slow order and the horn for workers, an emergency stop, a festival crowd.\n1515\t\n1516\t**S4 · SUNSET RUSH.** 17:30 sunset, clear, **`h8000-10`** (10-car marker), Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen, quad track.\n1517\t\n1518\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1519\t|---|---|---|\n1520\t| SHOTENGAI | — | 17:30:00 |\n1521\t| DAIGAKU-MAE | 17:31:55 | 17:32:15 |\n1522\t| SAKURA-KOEN | 17:34:05 | — |\n1523\t\n1524\t- Geometry: line speed 80 (city); curve R 800 R at 12,400–12,800; signals SG-S 12,170, B401 13,000, DG-H 13,500, DG-S 13,770, B403 14,400,\n1525\t  KO-H 15,100; curve R 1000 L at 14,000; horn board 14,350 (park path).\n1526\t- **Rival** Sky Liner on x +7:\n1527\t  - it leaves Shotengai 5 s after us;\n1528\t  - runs level with us to 12,800 (its driver Ren on the radio);\n1529\t  - pulls ahead at 95;\n1530\t  - passes Daigaku-mae;\n1531\t  - waits at Koen, where it arrives first and stands beside our platform (its driver waves).\n1532\t- **Door rush** at Daigaku-mae (+8 s). **Glare** from 13,750 to 14,600. Crowd level 3 at every stop. `oncoming` on x +14 at 14,800.\n1533\t- Teaches: train length and stop markers, making up lost time without speeding, staying calm beside a faster train.\n1534\t\n1535\t**S5 · THE LAST HALO.** 23:10 night, fog patches, `h8000-6`, Sakura-Koen → Hoshimi-dai → Kawasemi → Akari Central.\n1536\t\n1537\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1538\t|---|---|---|\n1539\t| SAKURA-KOEN | — | 23:10:00 |\n1540\t| HOSHIMI-DAI | 23:12:15 | 23:12:35 |\n1541\t| KAWASEMI | 23:14:35 | 23:14:55 |\n1542\t| AKARI CENTRAL | 23:17:05 | — |\n1543\t\n1544\t- Geometry:\n1545\t  - quad ends at 15,600; curve R 600 R at 15,700–16,100;\n1546\t  - climb 15‰ from 16,100 to 16,900, with **fog 16,200–16,800**;\n1547\t  - Hoshimi-dai at 17,100;\n1548\t  - descent 12‰ from 17,500 to 18,200; curve R 700 L at 17,800–18,100 (limit 70);\n1549\t  - Kawasemi at 18,800;\n1550\t  - horn board 19,100; river bridge 19,200–19,500;\n1551\t  - downtown from 19,900; overpass at 20,150; limit 45 at 20,200 (points);\n1552\t  - **home signal AK-H at 20,350 shows YY** (restricted 25 into the terminal);\n1553\t  - Akari Central at 20,600.\n1554\t- Events: `fog`; `oncoming` last train at 19,000 with **flash** (answer with the horn: +2 s); the platform finale (crowd and staff line up, everyone\n1555\t  bows).\n1556\t- Then the **ending** (§4.26).\n1557\t- Teaches: night driving, fog and trusting signals, the YY aspect; the story's close.\n1558\t\n1559\t**PR · PARALLEL RUN** (Duel and hub; also in Free Run). 12:00 day, clear, `h8000-6`, Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen on the quad track. All\n1560\tfour tracks run clockwise (\"the Drivers' Festival\").\n1561\t\n1562\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1563\t|---|---|---|\n1564\t| SHOTENGAI | — | 12:00:00 |\n1565\t| DAIGAKU-MAE | 12:01:55 | 12:02:15 |\n1566\t| SAKURA-KOEN | 12:04:05 | — |\n1567\t\n1568\t- Every track has its own signals, with identical block timing. No rival AI, door rush or glare.\n1569\t- In a session the score is the standings (higher wins). The round fits in 5 min with the card and results.\n1570\t\n1571\t### 5.4 Characters (Humanoid rigs for portraits and on-world figures; Blob for the mascot)\n1572\t\n1573\t| Character | Role | Look (`E.Humanoid` options) | Voice | Notes |\n1574\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1575\t| **Tetsuo Hoshino** | Chief Instructor, 38 years, last day | `build:'heroic'`, navy coat uniform, cap with a gold badge (`hat:{style:'cap',color:'#1a2a4a'}`), grey hair, white moustache (drawn at the portrait), white gloves | hoshino | dry, proverbial; never quite praises |\n1576\t| **Mika Aoba** | your conductor | navy uniform, cap, ponytail, armband | mika | warm, exclamation marks |\n1577\t| **Haro-kun** | Halo Line mascot | `E.Blob({ R: 7, colors: white/cream, wings: true, feet: true, mouth: true })` plus a drawn gold halo ring and headlight-eyes | haro | title, tips, PERFECT, attract host, boot screen |\n1578\t| **Station Master Ota** | Akari Central | grey coat, red-banded cap | ota | S5 finale |\n1579\t| **Kota** | train-fan kid at Hanabatake | small (`size:.8`), yellow cap, backpack, camera | kota | waves at every stop |\n1580\t| **Grandma Fuji** | regular at Okiku-dera/Yuhi-zaka | kimono colours, bun hair, `hunch` | fuji | bows |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"3279231d-ef66-4447-af65-b64ad3391afe","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:37.353Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Results:** both score cards side by side, then the winner's banner with Haro-kun cheering. Rematch / Title.\n\n**Tests:** `game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })`; both inputs drive their own trains; two viewports draw; two autopilots finish; the winner is the higher score;\na tie is shown as a tie.\n\n### 4.25 Settings, accessibility, difficulty\n\n**The game's own settings** (group `Game`, via `menu.settings` or Shell items):\n- Difficulty: Easy / Normal / Expert.\n- **Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox.** The default is PlayStation; its `apply` sets the standard `glyphs` setting.\n- Lever direction: Up = Power / Up = Brake.\n- Braking guide: On / Off (default On for Easy, Off otherwise).\n- Auto calls: Off / On.\n- Subtitles: On / Off (default On).\n- Show tips: On / Off.\n- Stop Cam: On / Off.\n- Cab display: Full / Minimal.\n- Driving music: Off / On.\n- Camera sway: 0–100%.\n\n**Standard settings** (built in; don't rebuild them): volume, music, effects, reduce motion (turns off sway and flashes), screen filter (CRT/scanlines),\ncontrols rebinding, rumble, and so on.\n\nEverything stays readable with no colour vision: signal letters, judgment words and lamp positions.\n\n**Tests:** each setting applies (glyph family, lever flip, guide visible, auto calls, subtitles off hides the subtitle box); settings survive a reload via\n`E.store`.\n\n### 4.26 Front-end screens (`55-ui-*.js`): big, few items, pixel-art, controller-first\n\n- **Title:**\n  - The background is the rail renderer's platform camera at Akari Central at dawn, with a Halo 8000 gliding in.\n  - Logo: `E.font.title('DENSHA DE HALO!', ...)` (scale 4, gold gradient) with a glowing gold **halo ring** around the final \"O\", and Haro-kun\n    bouncing beside it.\n  - Subtitle: \"THE HALO LINE · AKARI CITY\".\n  - `E.Menu`: CAREER · FREE RUN · DUEL · DRIVER'S LOG · HOW TO DRIVE · SETTINGS · ABOUT & CREDITS. Hover moves the focus and click picks.\n  - A prompt line with the device glyph, and the version (`E.versionLabel()` plus the game version v1.0).\n  - Keep it clear of the top-right corner buttons.\n- **Halo Map** (stage select):\n  - A gold ring (radius about 0.32 × min(W, H)) with 12 station dots and labels.\n  - Each stage is an arc between its stations: glowing when selected, grey when locked, with its rank stamp when done. Haro-kun floats in the centre.\n  - The stage card on the right (below on tall screens): name, time, weather, train, stops, best.\n  - ←/→ or the stick go round the ring; hover an arc to select it; ✕ or a click to go; ○ back.\n- **Free Run setup:** a stage on the ring, plus 4 rows of ←/→ choices (Time, Weather, Train, Difficulty), then START.\n- **Briefing:** §4.18.\n- **Results:**\n  - the rank stamp slams in (a scale tween, a shake, the stamp sound);\n  - 5 big lines (Stops, Punctuality, Calls & Horn, Smoothness, Penalties) with a total;\n  - Halo Time left; Hoshino's line;\n  - any new postcard flip;\n  - buttons: NEXT STAGE / RETRY / HALO MAP.\n- **Game Over:** the cracked halo; Hoshino's line; RETRY STAGE / CONTINUE FROM LAST STATION (Halo Time set back to the start value, score halved) / HALO MAP.\n- **Ending** (after S5's results):\n  - the finale cinematic: platform cam; staff and crowd bow; Hoshino gives you his pocket watch (dialog);\n  - then credits rolling over a night chase cam circling the whole ring, to \"Evening Halo\";\n  - \"THANK YOU FOR RIDING THE HALO LINE\";\n  - then the title, with S5 marked done.\n- **How to Drive:** a Shell `help` screen with keys for the current device and 5 short sections: Lever, Stop on the mark, Be on time, Point and\n  call, Signals & ATS.\n- **About & Credits:** pixel pages, ↑/↓ to scroll and ←/→ for the page, mouse wheel to scroll:\n  1. Credits (an original homage to *Densha de Go!* (Taito), not affiliated; my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato, MIT; the AI Hub client; asset sets if\n     used: Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG CC0; made by the building model);\n  2. **Source Information** (every TASK.md field);\n  3. Testing Feedback;\n  4. Engine Feedback;\n  5. Prompt Feedback.\n  - The text lives in `src/55-ui-about.js` and is filled in at the end, the same as the chat reply and `exit-interview.json` (§9).\n\n**Tests:** each screen opens and closes with confirm and cancel; the halo map wraps; locked stages can't be started; mouse hover selects (`input.feed('move')`);\nAbout contains every Source Information label; results buttons route correctly.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Content\n\n### 5.1 Akari City and the Halo Line\n\nThe line runs clockwise as a loop of **20,600 m** with **12 stations**. It is double-track: ours at x 0, the counter-clockwise track at x +3.8.\nFrom 11,800 to 15,600 it is **quad-track**: tracks at −7, 0, +7, +14; island platforms span −5.4…−1.6 and +8.6…+12.4. Line colours: **Halo Gold**\n`#f2c230` and **Sky** `#3aa0e0`.\n\n| # | id | In-game name | Meaning | Stop (6-car s) | Platform | Zone | Landmark / character |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | akari | AKARI CENTRAL | Akari Central | 0 (≡ 20,600) | island + side, 245 m, big roof | downtown | terminal hall with clock tower; Station Master Ota |\n| 1 | hanabatake | HANABATAKE | Flower Fields | 1,600 | left, 190 m | suburb-flowers | greenhouses, flower rows; Kota the train-fan kid |\n| 2 | kujira | KUJIRA-BASHI | Whale Bridge | 3,450 | right, 175 m | riverside | whale-back steel arch over the river mouth (bridge 2,600–3,200) |\n| 3 | minato | MINATO-MAE | Harbor Front | 5,100 | left + freight yard right | harbor | gantry cranes, containers, ferry; seagulls |\n| 4 | todai | TODAI-SHITA | Below the Lighthouse | 6,950 | island with passing loop | cliff | lighthouse on the cliff; tunnel 6,050–6,550 |\n| 5 | okiku | OKIKU-DERA | Great Chrysanthemum Temple | 8,700 | left, wooden, 185 m | temple-town | five-storey pagoda, temple gate, festival; Grandma Fuji |\n| 6 | yuhi | YUHI-ZAKA | Sunset Slope | 10,450 | right, hilltop | hills | terraced houses, sea view, little shrine |\n| 7 | shotengai | SHOTENGAI | Shopping Arcade | 12,100 | 2 islands (quad), viaduct | city-elevated | arcade roofs, neon game centre; Kenji's office |\n| 8 | daigaku | DAIGAKU-MAE | University | 13,700 | 2 islands (quad) | campus | clock tower, ginkgo trees, bicycles |\n| 9 | koen | SAKURA-KOEN | Cherry Blossom Park | 15,300 | 2 islands (quad) | park | sakura, pond, the \"Akari Eye\" Ferris wheel; petals |\n| 10 | hoshimi | HOSHIMI-DAI | Stargazing Heights | 17,100 | left | hills-north | observatory dome |\n| 11 | kawasemi | KAWASEMI | Kingfisher | 18,800 | right | river-north | river bridge 19,200–19,500, fishermen, paddies |\n\n- **Stop markers and platform lengths:**\n  - Akari Central and the three quad-section stations (Shotengai, Daigaku-mae, Sakura-Koen) have both \"6\" and \"10\" markers, with the 10 placed\n    8 m past the 6. Their platforms are 220–245 m.\n  - Every other station has only a \"6\" marker, on a platform of about 180 m.\n- **The quad transition (11,650–11,800):** the counter-clockwise track swings out from +3.8 to +14 in a gentle S-curve, and tracks −7 and +7 branch\n  off. Do the same in reverse at 15,600–15,750. In normal service, 0 and +7 carry clockwise trains (the Halo local and the Sky Liner express), and\n  −7 and +14 carry counter-clockwise ones.\n- **Station kit** (things and strips): name boards every 40 m (white; big romaji; English meaning smaller; previous and next stations with\n  arrows), canopy and columns, benches, vending machines (red/blue/white with lit panels), sorting bins, a platform clock, LED departure board,\n  stair housings, a safety fence, door-queue marks, staff at the head end, a Haro-kun poster.\n- In-game text is ASCII (the font has no kana or macrons), so names have no macrons: TODAI-SHITA, OKIKU-DERA, SHOTENGAI.\n\n**Zones** (scenery sets; buildings come from a parametric box generator, §5.6):\n\n| zone | s range | ground | buildings (weights) | nature | props | backdrop |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| downtown | 19,900–700 | concrete | office towers .4, department store .2, hotels .2, overpasses | street trees | billboards (Haro-kun ads), lamp posts, vending machines | city skyline |\n| suburb-flowers | 700–2,500 | fields/grass | houses .5 (blue/grey/terracotta roofs), apartments with balconies and laundry .3, greenhouses .1, konbini .1 | flower rows, paddies | utility poles and wires, bikes, crossing mirrors | hills, far city |\n| riverside | 2,500–3,600 | water/reeds | boat sheds | reeds, willows | fishermen, rowboats (library) | river mouth, sea |\n| harbor | 3,600–5,800 | asphalt | warehouses (long strips with roll-up doors) .5, container stacks .4 | — | gantry cranes, crates/barrels (library), bollards, seagulls | sea, ships |\n| cliff | 5,800–7,500 | rock/grass | fishing houses | pines (library), rocks | stone walls, tunnel portals | sea, cliffs |\n| temple-town | 7,500–9,300 | gravel | machiya (dark wood, tiled roofs) .6, shops with noren .4 | pines, maples, stone lanterns | lantern strings, torii, stalls | hills, pagoda |\n| hills | 9,300–11,700 | slopes | terrace houses | cedars, bamboo | retaining walls, guard rails | sea (left), sunset |\n| city-elevated | 11,700–13,200 | rooftops below the viaduct | arcade roofs, neon facades, apartment towers | — | sound walls, billboards | skyline |\n| campus | 13,200–14,500 | lawns | university blocks, gym dome | ginkgo | bike rows, students | city |\n| park | 14,500–16,000 | grass | pavilion | sakura (petal particles) | lanterns, benches (library) | hills, Ferris wheel |\n| hills-north | 16,000–18,000 | grass/forest | houses | cedars | poles | mountains, stars |\n| river-north | 18,000–19,700 | paddies/water | farmhouses | reeds | scarecrows, fishermen | mountains |\n| depot | depot route | gravel | depot sheds (strips), pits | — | lamps, workers, parked trains | dawn city |\n\n**Depot route** (S0): 1,000 m on a single track with sidings at x ±4.5 holding parked trains (0–350); straight to 400, a curve R 800 L from 400 to 600,\nthen straight. Stop marks (yellow boards) at 300, 620 and 900. A staff halt platform \"DEPOT GATE\" on the left at 860–920. A shunting signal at 40.\n\n### 5.2 Trains\n\n| id | name | cab | notches | traction a0 (km/h/s) | brakes | lags (apply/release/power) | vmax | sound | livery |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `h8000` | HALO 8000 | modern grey panel, one T-handle, LCD notch display | P5 / B8 | .8 1.4 2.0 2.6 3.2 (vk 15 25 35 40 45) | 0.5·n, EB 5.0 | .7 / .5 / .3 s | 110 | VVVF \"singing\" | silver, gold halo stripe, sky band |\n| `h3000` | HALO 3000 (retro) | green panel, two handles, analog gauges | P4 / B7 | .7 1.3 1.9 2.5 (vk 18 28 36 42) | 0.55·n, EB 4.6 | 1.1 / .8 / .5 s | 100 | resistor growl and clunks | cream, orange stripe |\n| `skyliner` | SKY LINER (rival) | — | AI | — | — | — | 120 | — | purple and silver |\n| `freight` | MINATO FREIGHT | — | AI | — | — | — | 75 | — | blue loco plus colourful containers |\n| `inner` | HALO 8000 inner loop | — | AI | — | — | — | — | — | as h8000 |\n\n- Formations: `h8000-6`, `h8000-10` (S4), `h3000-6` (S2).\n\n### 5.3 Stages\n\nTimes are initial values; calibrate them (§4.8). \"s\" means route metres.\n\n**S0 · DAWN DEPOT** (tutorial). 05:30 dawn, clear, `h8000-6`, depot route, Halo Time frozen.\n\nSteps, each a Hoshino line with a prompt; the next unlocks when the condition holds:\n1. P1, reach 10 km/h.\n2. N, coast.\n3. Brake: get below 5 km/h.\n4. Stop at Mark 1 (300); judged with no penalty; Stop Cam explained.\n5. The departure call on the shunting signal.\n6. Up to 40 under the \"40\" board.\n7. Mark 2 (620), easing to B1: SMOOTH explained.\n8. EB demo (pull, stop, release).\n9. Mark 3 (900) within 1 m to pass; retry the step on failure.\n\nThe certificate stamp follows, then S1 unlocks. Halo Time, ATS and the horn get one sentence each from Hoshino (\"You'll meet those in service\").\n\n**S1 · FIRST LIGHT LOCAL.** 06:40 dawn into morning, clear, `h8000-6`, Akari Central → Hanabatake → Kujira-bashi.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| AKARI CENTRAL | — | 06:40:00 |\n| HANABATAKE | 06:42:05 | 06:42:30 |\n| KUJIRA-BASHI | 06:44:45 | — |\n\nGeometry (route script excerpt, the pattern for every stage):\n```\n[-230,'station',{id:'akari',side:'island',len:245,stop:{6:0,10:8},roof:[-215,5],melody:'akari',crowd:3,landmark:'terminal'}]\n[0,'zone','downtown'] [60,'signal',{id:'AK-S',kind:'start'}] [150,'overpass',{w:18,h:7}]\n[200,'limit',{v:45,until:420}] [420,'limit',{v:85}] [520,'curve',{len:260,r:900,dir:'R'}]\n[700,'zone','suburb-flowers'] [700,'signal',{id:'B101',kind:'block'}]\n[880,'limit',{v:70,until:1260}] [900,'curve',{len:330,r:500,dir:'L'}]\n[1050,'horn',{}] [1110,'crossing',{id:'X1',road:6,cars:3,peds:2}] [1250,'signal',{id:'B102',kind:'block'}]\n[1380,'signal',{id:'HB-H',kind:'home'}] [1420,'station',{id:'hanabatake',side:'L',len:190,stop:{6:1600},melody:'hanabatake',crowd:2}]\n[1660,'signal',{id:'HB-S',kind:'start'}] [1800,'grade',{len:300,permille:8}] [2150,'signal',{id:'B103',kind:'block'}]\n[2300,'horn',{}] [2450,'limit',{v:75,until:3250}] [2500,'zone','riverside'] [2600,'bridge',{len:600,kind:'truss',water:'river'}]\n[2700,'curve',{len:400,r:1200,dir:'R'}] [2950,'signal',{id:'B104',kind:'block'}] [3250,'signal',{id:'KJ-H',kind:'home'}]\n[3290,'station',{id:'kujira',side:'R',len:175,stop:{6:3450},melody:'kujira',crowd:2}]\n```\n\n- Events: crossing X1 (normal); `oncoming` at 2,000; Kota waves at Hanabatake (dwell); radio lines (§5.5).\n- Teaches: the timetable and clock, the departure procedure, calls, the horn board, a limit board, an oncoming train, crossing bells, melodies and\n  announcements.\n\n**S2 · HARBOR RAIN RAPID.** 10:15 day, **rain**, `h3000-6`, Kujira-bashi → Minato-mae → (pass Todai-shita) → Okiku-dera.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| KUJIRA-BASHI | — | 10:15:00 |\n| MINATO-MAE | 10:16:55 | 10:17:20 |\n| TODAI-SHITA | pass 10:20:20 | |\n| OKIKU-DERA | 10:22:15 | — |\n\n- Geometry: line speed 95 (Rapid); curve R 700 L at 3,700–4,000 (limit 80).\n  - Signals: B201 3,900, B202 4,300, MN-H 4,880 (the Minato-mae platform runs 4,925–5,115), MN-S 5,160, **M5600** 5,600, **M6000** 6,000,\n    B205 6,600, TD-H 6,850 (main line through, no platform stop), B207 7,600, OK-H 8,480 (the Okiku-dera platform runs 8,530–8,715).\n  - Tunnel 6,050–6,550 with a curve R 400 R (limit 60, horn board 5,950).\n  - Pass board at 6,550. Freight loop at Todai-shita on the left, 6,750–7,150.\n- **Freight script** (260 m long):\n  - It joins our track from the Minato yard at 5,250 at **10:16:20** and runs at 45 km/h (12.5 m/s).\n  - It **stops with its front at 6,300 from about 10:17:44 for 40 s** (points being set), then pulls on and diverges into the Todai loop at 6,780,\n    where it stands.\n  - What the player gets, at par:\n    - At our 10:17:20 departure its rear is in block M5600–M6000, so the starting signal MN-S shows **Y** (call: \"Chui!\").\n    - Near 10:17:56 we pass M6000's ATS beacon at 5,400. M6000 is **R** (the freight is standing in block 6,000–6,600), so the **ATS bell rings**.\n    - We stop before M6000 at about 10:18:56. The freight pulls away at 10:18:24, and its rear clears 6,600 at about 10:19:25, so M6000 turns\n      **Y** after a wait of 20–30 s, then **G** once the freight is wholly in the loop (about 10:19:50).\n  - We see its tail lights through the rain while we arrive at Minato-mae, and later pass it standing in the loop at Todai-shita.\n  - The test (§4.4) checks this sequence with the autopilot.\n- Teaches: another train type (two handles, slow brakes), rain slip and slide, yellow signals, ATS confirm, a tunnel, a pass station.\n\n**S3 · TEMPLE HILL LOCAL.** 14:00 afternoon haze, clear, `h8000-6`, Okiku-dera → Yuhi-zaka → Shotengai. The stage **opens during the festival dwell**\nat Okiku-dera.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| OKIKU-DERA | (dwell) | 14:00:00 |\n| YUHI-ZAKA | 14:02:40 | 14:03:00 |\n| SHOTENGAI | 14:05:30 | — |\n\n- Geometry:\n  - crossing X2 at 9,050 (normal);\n  - climb **25‰** from 9,200 to 10,300; curve R 600 R at 9,300–9,600; curve R 450 L at 9,900–10,200 (limit 60);\n  - horn board 9,450; **workers** with a slow order of 25 from 9,600 to 9,900 (lookout at 9,550);\n  - Yuhi-zaka at 10,450;\n  - descent **20‰** from 10,700 to 11,450; curve R 500 L at 10,900–11,200 (limit 55);\n  - **obstruction emitter at 11,150 for crossing X3 at 11,500** (the festival's takoyaki cart); horn board 11,400;\n  - viaduct from 11,700; Shotengai at 12,100.\n- Events: festival (crowd ×2, lanterns, taiko), `workers`, `obstruction` at X3 (clears 12 s after we stop), Grandma Fuji bows at Yuhi-zaka, `oncoming`\n  at 11,200.\n- Teaches: gradients both ways, a slow order and the horn for workers, an emergency stop, a festival crowd.\n\n**S4 · SUNSET RUSH.** 17:30 sunset, clear, **`h8000-10`** (10-car marker), Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen, quad track.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHOTENGAI | — | 17:30:00 |\n| DAIGAKU-MAE | 17:31:55 | 17:32:15 |\n| SAKURA-KOEN | 17:34:05 | — |\n\n- Geometry: line speed 80 (city); curve R 800 R at 12,400–12,800; signals SG-S 12,170, B401 13,000, DG-H 13,500, DG-S 13,770, B403 14,400,\n  KO-H 15,100; curve R 1000 L at 14,000; horn board 14,350 (park path).\n- **Rival** Sky Liner on x +7:\n  - it leaves Shotengai 5 s after us;\n  - runs level with us to 12,800 (its driver Ren on the radio);\n  - pulls ahead at 95;\n  - passes Daigaku-mae;\n  - waits at Koen, where it arrives first and stands beside our platform (its driver waves).\n- **Door rush** at Daigaku-mae (+8 s). **Glare** from 13,750 to 14,600. Crowd level 3 at every stop. `oncoming` on x +14 at 14,800.\n- Teaches: train length and stop markers, making up lost time without speeding, staying calm beside a faster train.\n\n**S5 · THE LAST HALO.** 23:10 night, fog patches, `h8000-6`, Sakura-Koen → Hoshimi-dai → Kawasemi → Akari Central.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| SAKURA-KOEN | — | 23:10:00 |\n| HOSHIMI-DAI | 23:12:15 | 23:12:35 |\n| KAWASEMI | 23:14:35 | 23:14:55 |\n| AKARI CENTRAL | 23:17:05 | — |\n\n- Geometry:\n  - quad ends at 15,600; curve R 600 R at 15,700–16,100;\n  - climb 15‰ from 16,100 to 16,900, with **fog 16,200–16,800**;\n  - Hoshimi-dai at 17,100;\n  - descent 12‰ from 17,500 to 18,200; curve R 700 L at 17,800–18,100 (limit 70);\n  - Kawasemi at 18,800;\n  - horn board 19,100; river bridge 19,200–19,500;\n  - downtown from 19,900; overpass at 20,150; limit 45 at 20,200 (points);\n  - **home signal AK-H at 20,350 shows YY** (restricted 25 into the terminal);\n  - Akari Central at 20,600.\n- Events: `fog`; `oncoming` last train at 19,000 with **flash** (answer with the horn: +2 s); the platform finale (crowd and staff line up, everyone\n  bows).\n- Then the **ending** (§4.26).\n- Teaches: night driving, fog and trusting signals, the YY aspect; the story's close.\n\n**PR · PARALLEL RUN** (Duel and hub; also in Free Run). 12:00 day, clear, `h8000-6`, Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen on the quad track. All\nfour tracks run clockwise (\"the Drivers' Festival\").\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHOTENGAI | — | 12:00:00 |\n| DAIGAKU-MAE | 12:01:55 | 12:02:15 |\n| SAKURA-KOEN | 12:04:05 | — |\n\n- Every track has its own signals, with identical block timing. No rival AI, door rush or glare.\n- In a session the score is the standings (higher wins). The round fits in 5 min with the card and results.\n\n### 5.4 Characters (Humanoid rigs for portraits and on-world figures; Blob for the mascot)\n\n| Character | Role | Look (`E.Humanoid` options) | Voice | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Tetsuo Hoshino** | Chief Instructor, 38 years, last day | `build:'heroic'`, navy coat uniform, cap with a gold badge (`hat:{style:'cap',color:'#1a2a4a'}`), grey hair, white moustache (drawn at the portrait), white gloves | hoshino | dry, proverbial; never quite praises |\n| **Mika Aoba** | your conductor | navy uniform, cap, ponytail, armband | mika | warm, exclamation marks |\n| **Haro-kun** | Halo Line mascot | `E.Blob({ R: 7, colors: white/cream, wings: true, feet: true, mouth: true })` plus a drawn gold halo ring and headlight-eyes | haro | title, tips, PERFECT, attract host, boot screen |\n| **Station Master Ota** | Akari Central | grey coat, red-banded cap | ota | S5 finale |\n| **Kota** | train-fan kid at Hanabatake | small (`size:.8`), yellow cap, backpack, camera | kota | waves at every stop |\n| **Grandma Fuji** | regular at Okiku-dera/Yuhi-zaka | kimono colours, bun hair, `hunch` | fuji | bows |","numLines":300,"startLine":1281,"totalLines":1952}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QkyBMSZ7rBvkcT4GqhwjmH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
