{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwgKcomV9X3YrPDUoBh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the About text is left failing. I'll write the About pages with the Source Information and the three feedback sets as the plan requires, and add a page listing what this build leaves out, so the credits don't overstate it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":657377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"12c6adf7-4186-4f13-8deb-5c93b9807f94","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:10:53.893Z","request_id":"req_011CghwgKDVf7r5Bu4xXR3Dj"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwgKcomV9X3YrPDUoBh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YUuwZ2BpMZB3a8pdVsgTpU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('src/61-drive.js').read()\ni=s.index(\"/* About & Credits: the pages\")\nj=s.index(\"})();\", i)\nnew='''/* About & Credits (section 4.26, 9.5): the credits, the Source Information, the three feedback sets, and what this build\n * does not include. Written at the end of the build; the same text is in the chat reply and exit-interview.json. */\nDH.ABOUT = [\n  { title: 'CREDITS', lines: ['DENSHA DE HALO!', 'An original homage to Densha de Go! (Taito). Not affiliated.', 'Built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the engine, MIT License) by Michael Crosato.', 'AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0 (AI Hub).', 'Made by claude-haiku-5-5 (Claude Code, headless).'] },\n  { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:41', 'Source: Densha de Go! (Taito)', 'Plan: PLAN.md',\n    'Genre: train driving simulation with arcade scoring. Perspective: first-person cab view (pseudo-3D), with chase and platform cameras and a Halo Map.',\n    'Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, handoff package) with a custom rail renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.',\n    'Art: the engine\\\\'s pixel style; new code-drawn trains, cab, signals, stations and townscape.',\n    'Animation: code-tweened gloved call, gates, needle, notch cells and judgment banners. Character rigs are not drawn in play.',\n    'Audio: all procedural: Web Audio traction, rolling, wind and brake layers, chip sound effects, 12 departure melodies, gibberish voices (syllable synthesis).',\n    'Online: AI Hub session, ghost mode, 2 to 4 players (protocol v1).', 'Testing: headless suites (node test/run.mjs), a mock hub contract, the scripted playthrough and Playwright browser checks.',\n    'Research: the engine handoff docs and the AI Hub protocol; no web research.', 'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium for the browser checks.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.', 'Usage: unknown.'] },\n  { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', lines: [\n    'Issues caught: about twenty changed the code, from rail drawing and the autopilot to the timetable and halo start.',\n    'Critical: about six. The rail drew nothing; the autopilot stuck in EB; the halo started at zero; a permanent 25 km/h cap; strips only on their first segment; parked trains left the blocks.',\n    'Most helpful: the stop-accuracy runs from several start states (the last metres of every approach).',\n    'Least helpful: the stub draw and the screenshots: they catch exceptions and layout, not feel.'] },\n  { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the fixed step with game.advance, the scenes, the pixel primitives and the Dialog and Menu.',\n    'Stuck or guessed: the road module is a fork candidate, not a fit (it needs multiple tracks and strips); the settings-group filter was not used; scene data for game.start was unclear.',\n    'Built myself: the rail renderer, the train model, the signal and stop logic, the autopilot, the dev sliders.',\n    'Hardest: projection and occlusion for long strips; the font has no button symbols and no middle dot.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. Dev Mode and settings are our own screens.',\n    'One change: a font with common UI symbols, and a documented settings-group filter for dev screens.'] },\n  { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the plan with checkable numbers (the check values made the physics testable).',\n    'Confusing: the scope (about fifty subsystems) against one session; the plan and TASK disagree on file layout in places.',\n    'Hardest: getting an end-to-end game with tests in one session; several features had to be cut.',\n    'Change: a priority order, with a minimum to ship, and a time budget per milestone.'] },\n  { title: 'NOT IN THIS BUILD', lines: [\n    'Local two-player duel (split screen). Only the hub ghost mode is built.',\n    'The Stop Cam after each stop, the trackside camera, the Halo 3000 cab art, the lever direction setting.',\n    'Driver\\\\'s Log postcards and the stats page is partial; the Halo Map shows records only as stamps.',\n    'Character rigs in play, the shunting and crowd animation, the duel and the hub card art are simpler than planned.',\n    'Calibrated stops and timetables are from the autopilot, not from human play.'] }\n];\n\n'''\ns=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\nopen('src/61-drive.js','w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nnode -e \"new (require('vm').Script)(require('fs').readFileSync('src/61-drive.js','utf8'))\" && node tools/bundle.mjs >/dev/null && timeout 600 node test/run.mjs game 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Write About pages with Source Information and feedback"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":657377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1723},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"2cd4dfc8-9db6-40ca-8605-29fff974bf80","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:11:02.186Z","request_id":"req_011CghwgKDVf7r5Bu4xXR3Dj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YUuwZ2BpMZB3a8pdVsgTpU":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work/DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050241 && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('src/61-drive.js').read()\ni=s.index(\"/* About & Credits: the pages\")\nj=s.index(\"})();\", i)\nnew='''/* About & Credits (section 4.26, 9.5): the credits, the Sour