{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghwhw15PMWBTHNBk7gsT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014gZT7QRdCCGLmUqMVposMk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:41\",\n    \"source\": \"Densha de Go! (Taito)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Train driving simulation with arcade scoring\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First-person cab view (pseudo-3D), with chase and platform cameras, and a Halo Map for stage select\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, handoff package) with a custom rail renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era pixel style; new code-drawn trains, cab, signals, stations and townscape\",\n    \"animation\": \"Code-tweened gloved call, crossing gates, speed needle, notch cells and judgment banners; character rigs are not drawn in play\",\n    \"audio\": \"All procedural: Web Audio traction, rolling, wind and brake layers; chip sound effects; 12 departure melodies; gibberish voices by syllable synthesis\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub session, ghost mode, 2 to 4 players (Session Protocol 1)\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless suites via one command (node test/run.mjs), a mock AI Hub contract, a scripted autopilot playthrough of every stage, and Playwright browser checks\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the engine handoff docs and the AI Hub protocol; no web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium via Playwright for the browser checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About twenty issues changed the code, from rail drawing and the autopilot to the timetable and the Halo Time start value.\",\n    \"About six were critical: the rail drew nothing; the autopilot got stuck in emergency braking; Halo Time started at zero; a permanent 25 km/h cap; strips were attached only to their first segment; parked trains left the blocks.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was the stop-accuracy runs from several starting states, which exposed the planner's last-metre errors.\",\n    \"The least helpful were the stub draw and the screenshot checks: they catch exceptions and layout, not how the game feels.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The fixed step with game.advance, the scene system, the pixel primitives, E.Dialog and E.Menu.\",\n    \"The road module is a candidate to fork, not a fit (it needs several tracks and long strips). The settings-group filter was not used. Scene data for game.start was unclear.\",\n    \"The rail renderer, the train model, the signal and stop logic, the autopilot and the dev sliders: all built here.\",\n    \"Projection and occlusion for long strips; the font has no button symbols and no middle dot, so those were drawn or replaced.\",\n    \"Nothing in the engine was changed. Dev Mode and the settings are the game's own screens.\",\n    \"A font with common UI symbols, and a documented settings-group filter for dev screens.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan with checkable numbers: the check values made the physics testable.\",\n    \"The scope (about fifty subsystems) against one session, and the plan and TASK disagree on file layout in places.\",\n    \"Getting an end-to-end game with tests in one session; several features had to be cut.\",\n    \"A priority order with a minimum to ship, and a time budget per milestone.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Densha de Halo!\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Stop on the mark. Leave on the second.\",\n    \"description\": \"Drive the Halo Line, a loop railway around Akari City, from the first train at dawn to the last train at night: stop exactly on the mark, keep the timetable to the second, and point and call every signal. Race up to three friends on the four-track Parallel Run.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Simulation\",\n    \"source\": \"Densha de Go!\",\n    \"series\": \"Densha de Go!\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lever W/S or L2/R2 · Call E/✕ · Horn Space/□ · ATS Q/△ · EB Backspace/L1\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"retro\", \"versus\", \"story\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log('parses; keys', Object.keys(j).join(','), 'sourceFields', Object.keys(j.sourceInformation).length, 'hub', Object.keys(j.aiHub).length)\"","description":"Write exit-interview.json and verify it parses"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4293,"cache_read_input_tokens":659100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4293},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"9dc22b50-5c3e-4e8c-83be-008b10f76436","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:11:14.457Z","request_id":"req_011CghwhvbkhZeLKDwp9RqFu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014gZT7QRdCCGLmUqMVposMk":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:41\",\n    \"source\": \"Densha de Go! (Taito)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Train driving simulation with arcade scoring\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First-person cab view (pseudo-3D), with chase and platform cameras, and a Halo Map for stage select\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, handoff package) with a custom rail renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era pixel style; new code-drawn trains, cab, signals, stations and townscape\",\n    \"animation\": \"Code-tweened gloved call, crossing gates, speed needle, notch cells and judgment banners; character rigs are not drawn in play\",\n    \"audio\": \"All procedural: Web Audio traction, rolling, wind and brake layers; chip sound effects; 12 departure melodies; gibberish voices by syllable synthesis\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub session, ghost mode, 2 to 4 players (Session Protocol 1)\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless suites via one command (node test/run.mjs), a mock AI Hub contract, a scripted autopilot playthrough of every stage, and Playwright browser checks\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the engine handoff docs and the AI Hub protocol; no web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium via Playwright for the browser checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About twenty issues changed the code, from rail drawing and the autopilot to the timetable and the Halo Time start value.\",\n    \"About six were critical: the rail drew nothing; the autopilot got stuck in emergency braking; Halo Time started at zero; a permanent 25 km/h cap; strips were attached only to their first segment; parked trains left the blocks.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was the stop-accuracy runs from several starting states, which exposed the planner's last-metre errors.\",\n    \"The least helpful were the stub draw and the screenshot checks: they catch exceptions and layout, not how the game feels.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The fixed step with game.advance, the scene system, the pixel primitives, E.Dialog and E.Menu.\",\n    \"The road module is a candidate to fork, not a fit (it needs several tracks and long strips). The settings-group filter was not used. Scene data for game.start was unclear.\",\n    \"The rail renderer, the train model, the signal and stop logic, the autopilot and the dev sliders: all built here.\",\n    \"Projection and occlusion for long strips; the font has no button symbols and no middle dot, so those were drawn or replaced.\",\n    \"Nothing in the engine was changed. Dev Mode and the settings are the game's own screens.\",\n    \"A font with common UI symbols, and a documented settings-group filter for dev screens.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan with checkable numbers: the check values made the physics testable.\",\n    \"The scope (about fifty subsystems) against one session, and the plan and TASK disagree on file layout in places.\",\n    \"Getting an end-to-end game with tests in one session; several features had to be cut.\",\n    \"A priority order with a minimum to ship, and a time budget per milestone.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Densha de Halo!\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Stop on the mark. Leave on the second.\",\n    \"description\": \"Drive the Halo Line, a loop railway around Akari City, from the first train at dawn to the last train at night: stop exactly on the mark, keep the timetable to the second, and point and call every signal. Race up to three friends on the four-track Parallel Run.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Simulation\",\n    \"source\": \"Densha de Go!\",\n    \"series\": \"Densha de Go!\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lever W/S or L2/R2 · Call E/✕ · Horn Space/□ · ATS Q/△ · EB Backspace/L1\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"retro\", \"versus\", \"story\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log('parses; keys', Object.keys(j).join(','), 