{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghx27S91y8iVTvu5YYfn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is built and the test suite passes, but it does not meet the full TASK.md scope. Several features are missing, listed below.\n\n**Deliverables** (in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050241__xd92716/work/`)\n- `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050241.html`: the single-file bundle, 1.4 MB, with the hub client first and no external URLs.\n- `exit-interview.json`: parses, with every field filled.\n- Dev folder `DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050241/`: source, tools, tests, `NOTES.md`, `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` (no engine edits).\n\n**What works**\n- Title \"Densha de Halo!\", on a Japanese-style Halo Line loop with 12 stations, four trains, signals and ATS, speed limits, stops judged against the mark, timetables, dwell and departure, Halo Time, score, ranks, and calls and horn.\n- Stages S1 to S5 and the Parallel Run are all data-driven. Timetables were calibrated from the autopilot's minimum-time run plus 9 s.\n- Autopilot runs each stage to completion with no game over. Stops land within 0.05 m from the tested approach states.\n- Attract mode (after 10 s idle), touch-only message, Dev Mode with live sliders and reset, and PlayStation/Xbox prompts.\n- AI Hub ghost mode: ready with no input, play gated on the hub clock, send rate about 3 per second, one result, a silent end. A mock hub test checks this contract; I did not run the real hub harness.\n- Test command: `node test/run.mjs --browser` gives 121 passed, 0 failed, including the scripted playthrough and browser checks. I re-ran the fast suites after the last edit and they still pass (97 passed).\n\n**What is missing or only partial**\n- No local two-player duel or split screen.\n- No Stop Cam, trackside camera, lever-direction setting, Halo 3000 cab art, or postcards.\n- No tips system beyond a few subtitle lines.\n- Stage S0 is only the three marks with frozen Halo Time; the step-by-step lessons are not implemented.\n- Character rigs are not drawn in play, and the crowd and staff animation is not there.\n- The Driver's Log shows records and stats only, and the Dev Mode sound board is minimal.\n- Hub: no hub card art beyond a text card, no name tags on ghost trains, and the pause menu is not restricted in sessions.\n- The Stop hook is still active, so ending this turn won't release it. The goal condition is not fully satisfied, mainly by the missing duel and the other gaps above.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:41\n- Source: Densha de Go! (Taito)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: train driving simulation with arcade scoring\n- Perspective: first-person cab (pseudo-3D), with chase and platform cameras and a Halo Map\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, handoff package) with a custom rail renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- Art Direction: the engine's pixel style with new code-drawn trains, cab, signals, stations and townscape\n- Animation: code-tweened gloved call, crossing gates, needle, notch cells and judgment banners; no character rigs in play\n- Audio: all procedural (Web Audio layers, chip effects, 12 melodies, syllable-synthesis voices)\n- Online: AI Hub session, ghost mode, 2 to 4 players (protocol v1)\n- Testing: one headless command plus Playwright browser checks, a mock hub contract, and a scripted playthrough\n- Research: engine handoff docs and AI Hub protocol; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium for the browser checks\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues caught: about twenty changed the code.\n- Critical: about six, including the rail drawing nothing, the autopilot stuck in emergency braking, Halo Time starting at zero, a permanent 25 km/h cap, strips attached only to their first segment, and parked trains leaving the blocks.\n- Most helpful: the stop-accuracy runs from several starting states.\n- Least helpful: the no-op draw and the screenshots, which catch exceptions and layout but not feel.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the fixed step with `game.advance`, the scenes, the pixel primitives, and Dialog and Menu.\n- Stuck or guessed: the road module needed a fork rather than a drop-in use; the settings-group filter wasn't used; scene data for `game.start` was unclear.\n- Built myself: the rail renderer, the train model, the signal and stop logic, the autopilot, and the dev sliders.\n- Hardest: projection and occlusion for long strips; the font lacks button symbols and the middle dot.\n- Changed in the engine: nothing.\n- One change I'd want: a font with common UI symbols, and a documented settings-group filter for dev screens.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the plan's checkable numbers, which made the physics testable.\n- Confusing: the scope (about fifty subsystems) against one session, and the plan and TASK disagree on file layout in places.\n- Hardest: getting an end-to-end game with tests in one session; several features had to be cut.\n- Change: a priority order with a minimum to ship, and a time budget per milestone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":688839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":846},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed18f8de-7c3c-4ed5-a440-ff3ec45bd88d","uuid":"8e99599e-1526-4a64-88af-92e380b35215","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:15:20.878Z","request_id":"req_011Cghx272aGiLeNmkXhrBmH"}
